complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118338447__7084\n\nXceltium is seeking an experienced Data Platform Administrator to own and advance our Microsoft data landscape. In this hands‑on role, you’ll administer databases, optimize performance, manage security, and support deployments within Azure data services and related platforms.\nYou’ll work with SQL Server, Azure SQL, and Microsoft Dataverse as we evolve Dynamics 365 data environments and related cloud technologies, shaping a scalable, well‑governed data foundation for our applications and AI","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"azure-data-platform-engineer-ai-automation-xceltium-tepa6hr7","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118338447__7084","source_posted_at":"2026-08-11T10:01:22Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"1daf9d13-b18c-53ab-8503-fea27f635edd","company_id":"f9513e98-d01b-5dbb-a535-b3619f31b4a2","title":"AI Engineer","location":"Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118063190__7084\n\nWe are looking for a mid-level to strong, hands-on AI Engineer who can build modern AI applications end to end - not research-heavy profiles, or generic data science candidates.\nWe need a pragmatic builder who has personally designed, deployed, and operated production-style GenAI solutions and can clearly explain their architecture, memory/state design, trade-offs, and implementation challenges.\nThis is a hands-on technical delivery role within our client's Data Engineering division. You will design, build, and operate enterprise-grade AI capabilities—specifically LLM-powered and retrieval-based experiences—ensuring they move beyond POC into sustained production.\nWhat You Will Do\n\n• LLM & GenAI Application Engineering: Build and operate enterprise LLM/GenAI solutions seamlessly integrated with Snowflake as the core data platform.\n• Production RAG & Agentic Workflows: Implement robust RAG","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"ai-engineer-jenkin-beattie-nzvzkd5g","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118063190__7084","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T15:01:18Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"a1e5dab0-fd3b-5a90-aec8-10d60716ce15","company_id":"a41237d8-31b0-56ba-8d98-e150e1e6f637","title":"AI Software Engineer – LLM, RAG & Cloud Apps","location":"Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118051844__7084\n\nDoghouse Agency seeks a Software Engineer (Artificial Intelligence) to design, develop and support production software across SaaS products and client platforms in Australia. The role focuses on secure, scalable cloud-native solutions using modern engineering practices.\nResponsibilities include building RAG pipelines, semantic search services, and embedding-based retrieval systems, while integrating OpenAI/other LLMs, vector databases, and orchestration frameworks.","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"ai-software-engineer-llm-rag-cloud-apps-doghouse-upz6msex","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118051844__7084","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T15:01:15Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"0abfaf12-e780-5e8e-a4be-2439549c83a5","company_id":"1cb94281-aeaf-5a6e-8156-43095121ebbc","title":"Data / ML Engineer","location":"New South Wales, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118618232__7084?geoID=2\n\nWe wrap our arms around businesses and help them scale. We work with enterprises and fast-growing companies to implement AI strategy, workflow automation, and build custom software. Not as a vendor, but as a genuine partner with skin in the game.\nWe move at a pace most businesses have never experienced, and we hold ourselves to a standard most agencies can't match. We don't pitch solutions. We sit with our clients, understand where they're stuck, and build the systems that get them unstuck. Quickly and properly.\nThe work is the kind engineers actually want: agent-first platforms running national field operations at around 90% automation, electric vehicle operating systems for everything from cars to trucks and buses, AI making real operational decisions in regulated industries, and rescues of platforms other teams couldn't deliver. And for the right businesses we go further. We unlock them: we build new products we come up with together, and we bring","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"data-ml-engineer-10x-labs-vu5uhutl","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118618232__7084?geoID=2","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:19Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"dbed39c3-fbce-5466-bb7b-bd9cd09ac19e","company_id":"2292015f-6696-5d43-af9a-9d7e5313309b","title":"Production AI Engineer: Build Real-World AI Apps","location":"New South Wales, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118010237__7084?geoID=2\n\nGalileo Search in Australia is hiring 3 Forward Deployed AI Engineers to turn unclear business problems into production systems. You will work directly with users, write code, and own the path from first workflow to measurable adoption.\nYou will design, build and deploy full‑stack AI applications, integrate with enterprise data, and help customers move quickly from prototype to production while ensuring security, observability and governance.","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"production-ai-engineer-build-real-world-ai-apps-galileo-search-7oqirmoj","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118010237__7084?geoID=2","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:19Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"bc75d235-fb04-51b5-9bae-a03d76280fab","company_id":"8e983689-7ac7-59b7-940c-3d6ce12dec26","title":"Machine Learning Engineer","location":"Perth, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118074941__7084?geoID=1943\n\nJob Summary\n\nJoin a global mining technology leader as a Machine Learning Engineer focused on evaluating, benchmarking and improving the performance of LLM and agent-based AI systems.\n\nYou’ll develop evaluation frameworks, measure model effectiveness and help ensure our AI solutions deliver reliable, scalable outcomes for customers across the mining industry while contributing to the ongoing evolution of our AI capabilities.\n\nKey Selling Points\n\n• Build AI and machine learning solutions from the ground up.\n\n• Work with cutting-edge technologies.\n\n• Join a global mining technology business.\n\nAbout Us\n\nWe are a global mining software business bringing together the expertise of Micromine, Motion Metrics and Fast2Mine.\n\nOur solutions help mining companies explore, design, plan and operate more effectively through industry-leading software, AI, machine vision and automation technologies. From geology and mine","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"machine-learning-engineer-micromine-kprqt52w","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118074941__7084?geoID=1943","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:18Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"ab05c6b7-927c-5949-b29a-65a488d1afb5","company_id":"10b293d3-08d0-59b5-af48-420bad3ff273","title":"Consultant, AI Engineer","location":"Victoria, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118128017__7084?geoID=7\n\nAt NAB we are using AI to reimagine banking and create better customer outcomes for our customers and colleagues. We have several exciting opportunities for AI Engineers to join our team to help build the next generation of intelligent solutions that operate at enterprise level.\n\nHighlights\n\n• Build the future of Banking with AI.\n\n• Turn AI innovation into real world impact.\n\n• Create intelligent solutions for millions of customers.\n\nOur people are customer obsessed. They prioritise the needs and satisfaction of the customer above all else. Our mindset fosters innovation and creates strong, lasting customer relationships as we strive to be the most customer centric company in Australia and New Zealand.\n\nIn the role of Consultant - AI Engineer, you will join the AI Engineering and Research lab team as part of the broader AI Platforms team that’s doubling down on customer obsession.\n\nIn This Consultant AI Engineer","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"consultant-ai-engineer-nab-qhjk7sng","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118128017__7084?geoID=7","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:18Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"8448d3aa-b4f2-52fc-be7e-aded61c8bdc5","company_id":"5aa89a20-20ea-5cb6-be26-ead65581c218","title":"AI Engineer","location":"Australian Capital Territory, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118074897__7084?geoID=1\n\nLocation: ACT and all other major cities of Australia\nContract: 12 Months + 2 x 12 Month Extension Options\nSecurity Clearance: NV1 Security Clearance Mandatory\nCitizenship: Australian Citizenship Mandatory\nAbout the Role\nWe are seeking an experienced AI Engineer to design, develop and implement secure, scalable and governed Artificial Intelligence solutions within a federal government environment. This role will work closely with business stakeholders, cyber security specialists, architects and data professionals to deliver innovative AI-enabled services that improve business outcomes, enhance service delivery and align with government governance and security requirements. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to enterprise AI initiatives leveraging the latest Microsoft technologies, agentic AI frameworks and automation capabilities.\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Design, develop and deploy AI","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"ai-engineer-ignite-services-bzumthyp","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118074897__7084?geoID=1","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:18Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"30fe44ac-f9fb-5f08-8d78-3233a5704966","company_id":"0593e746-30a8-53bf-b6a3-c07abdc6d4ec","title":"AI Engineer","location":"Canberra, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118075164__7084?geoID=471\n\nSenior AI Engineer\n\nContract duration – 12-month contract with potential extension\n\nLocation of work – ACT\n\nSecurity Clearance – Must be able to obtain Negative Vetting Level 1\n\nDFP Recruitment is seeking an experienced Senior AI Engineer to join a high-profile federal government project focused on delivering secure, scalable and responsible AI solutions. In this role, you will design, develop and implement enterprise AI capabilities using Microsoft technologies, including Azure AI Foundry, Azure OpenAI, Copilot Studio and AI Agents. You will work with business stakeholders, cyber security teams, architects and data specialists to deliver innovative AI-enabled services that improve productivity, decision-making and service delivery.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Design, develop and deploy enterprise AI solutions and agentic applications.\n\n• Build and maintain Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) solutions, AI","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"ai-engineer-dfp-recruitment-soo5dugd","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118075164__7084?geoID=471","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:18Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"a2f82837-7323-5c35-b3cf-1a17ee69e414","company_id":"54199924-361b-57ca-bf0e-4382e0e00539","title":"AI Engineer: Build Scalable AI for Retail Growth","location":"Victoria, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118089263__7084?geoID=7\n\nBunnings is seeking an experienced AI Engineer to join the Data, AI & Loyalty team, building AI-enabled solutions that add real business value.\nYou’ll work with Python/C#/Scala, cloud platforms, and collaborate with product, engineering, and data teams to deliver scalable, measurable outcomes.\nThis hands-on role offers learning, mentoring, and opportunities to influence across the organisation.","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"ai-engineer-build-scalable-ai-for-retail-growth-bunnings-group-jkxeb2ae","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118089263__7084?geoID=7","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:18Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"d600d5a3-852a-5b39-9dd5-32af9b9f7574","company_id":"07a5df2b-d7d2-5f52-bb4a-a8644b598822","title":"Artificial Intelligence / Machine Learning Engineer","location":"Canberra, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118616969__7084?geoID=471\n\n• AI/ML engineering experience developing machine learning models within complex engineering environments\n• Permanent Full-Time\n• Based in Canberra - onsite\n• Must hold a current NV1 Security Clearance\nOur Client\nOur client aims to reinvent tomorrow by solving the world's most critical problems for thriving cities, resilient environments, mission-critical outcomes, operational advancement, scientific discovery and cutting-edge manufacturing, turning abstract ideas into realities that transform the world for good. Our client provides a full spectrum of professional services including consulting, technical, scientific and project delivery for the government and private sector.\nThe Role\nAn exciting opportunity exists for an experienced AI/ML Engineer to provide technical leadership across cutting-edge programs. You will support the development of AI/ML capability, influence future policy and","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"artificial-intelligence-machine-learning-engineer-talent-yfzw2f7i","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118616969__7084?geoID=471","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:16Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"7ab798d0-2c4c-5265-aa04-9a7f81703ebe","company_id":"3a942c0f-933b-5d51-819c-86b156d85879","title":"Machine Learning Engineer","location":"New South Wales, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118614079__7084?geoID=2\n\nTimescapes is looking for a Machine Learning Engineer to join our small, but growing team of high-performers. We’re after someone who approaches problems from first principles, honing in on underlying causes and diligently iterating towards the best solution. We believe that great products feature incredible experiences that customers never want to stop using.\n\nAbout us\n\nFounded in New Zealand in 2017, Timescapes is a visual progress tracking solution for complex construction projects – our mission is to simplify construction through shared visibility. Customers value Timescapes because it helps them stay on schedule, validate construction claims and communicate progress more effectively.\n\nWe’re a rapidly growing company, and are used by some of the largest construction firms across Australia, Canada, New Zealand and the United States. We’re deliberate and thoughtful in everything that we do, and we emphasise awareness, speed and quality in our approach to","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"machine-learning-engineer-timescapes-ltd-fpqco7xk","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__118614079__7084?geoID=2","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:15Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"76400a91-4d96-5422-8211-6de6fa805bc8","company_id":"2c62d6e2-f186-570a-88f7-52fe812d97a0","title":"AI Engineer","location":"Victoria, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"AI & Software","career_id":"ml-engineer","experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from freehire:whatjobs-au; read the complete posting at https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__119341006__7084?geoID=7\n\nChemist Warehouse is Australia’s largest pharmacy retailer with over 17,000 team members and more than 600 stores nationwide. Following our merger with Sigma Healthcare, we’re now a Top 50 ASX-listed company with expanding operations across New Zealand, Ireland, and China.\n\nTogether, we’re transforming healthcare and retail with industry-leading distribution, technology, and people practices — and we want you to be part of this journey.\n\nAbout us\n\nChemist Warehouse is Australia’s largest pharmacy retailer with over 17,000 team members and more than 600 stores nationwide. Following our merger with Sigma Healthcare, we’re now a Top 50 ASX-listed company with expanding operations across New Zealand, Ireland, and China.\n\nTogether, we’re transforming healthcare and retail with industry-leading distribution, technology, and people practices — and we want you to be part of this journey.\n\nAbout the role\n\nThe AI Engineer is responsible for","source_board":"freehire:whatjobs-au","source_external_id":"ai-engineer-chemist-warehouse-5yiojpwz","source_url":"https://au.whatjobs.com/pub_api__cpl__119341006__7084?geoID=7","source_posted_at":"2026-08-10T14:02:15Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"ai_engineer"},{"id":"03419fe4-e6e5-50e8-b144-5c9d5d417bb3","company_id":"f9ab1ff4-8241-5225-bda0-47b85659c9bf","title":"Finance Analyst","location":"Brisbane, QLD, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"3 years minimum","description":"Are you a commercially minded finance professional who thrives on turning data into business insights? Join Downer's Rail & Transit Systems team as a Finance Analyst and play a key role in driving financial performance, strategic decision-making, and operational excellence across our Queensland operations. \nReporting to the Commercial Finance Manager, you'll partner closely with operational and leadership teams to deliver budgeting, forecasting, financial modelling, performance reporting, and commercial analysis that supports business growth and profitability. You'll also identify cost-saving opportunities, improve financial processes, and help shape informed business decisions through meaningful financial insights\nThis fulltime permanent position is based in our Brisbane CBD office. \nAbout You:\n\n• \nDegree qualifications in Finance, Accounting or a related discipline. \n• \n3+ years experience in management accounting, commercial finance, budgeting and forecasting. \n• \nStrong financial modelling and analytical capability. \n• \nProven ability to influence stakeholders and translate complex financial data into actionable insights. \n• \nAdvanced Excel skills and a continuous improvement mindset. \n• \nExperience within rail, heavy industry or asset-intensive environments will be highly regarded.\n\nOur Culture:\nWe cultivate a diverse and inclusive workplace that facilitates opportunity and respect. Our focus on gender and cultural inclusiveness is active and ongoing, and through various initiatives we aim to help close the gap between indigenous and non-indigenous communities.\n\nWhat We Offer:\n\n• Career progression and development opportunities \n• A workplace focused on Zero Harm; safety is at the core of everything we do\n• Flexible working arrangements to encourage work/life balance \n• Competitive remuneration\n\nFor more details about this position contact Sarah Clark - Talent & Sourcing Business Partner, at sarah.clark@Downergroup.com\n\nPlease note applications will not be accepted via email, please apply via the link.\n\nYou want your work to matter and so do we. With over 26,000 people across Australia, New Zealand and the Pacific, our team is made up of individuals with unique perspectives, backgrounds, and ideas.\nWe know that diversity makes us stronger and we actively celebrate it through our commitment to inclusion and belonging. \nWe’re committed to building a team that reflects the diverse communities we serve and we welcome people of all ages, genders, sexual orientations, cultures, abilities, and lived experiences. We especially encourage applications from those whose voices have traditionally been underrepresented in our industry, including women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples, Māori and Pasifika Peoples, veterans, people with disability, and neurodivergent individuals. Even if your experience doesn’t align perfectly with this role, we’d still like to hear from you. If it feels like the right fit, apply - potential counts, and so do you. \nAs a WORK180 Endorsed Employer, we support flexibility that works for your life, inclusive leadership that values your voice, and equitable access to opportunity so you can do your best work and bring your whole self to it. \nIf you need support or adjustments through the recruitment process, just let us know, we’re here to help you put your best foot forward.","source_board":"freehire:oracle","source_external_id":"finance-analyst-downer-yfylegwe","source_url":"https://fa-exfs-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CareersAtDowner/job/736429","source_posted_at":"2026-09-15T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"c18d5199-185b-53fb-a44e-f3a9ec87e13b","company_id":"ee791455-9862-5d54-9013-f3b662d999da","title":"FP&A Analyst","location":"Sydney, NSW, AU","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"1 years minimum","description":"Sydney CBD | Full-Time | On-Site (5 Days)\nWHO WE AREFounded in 2013 as Scape Australia, leaders in student housing, we've since grown into a vertically integrated living platform known as The Living Company; managing $18B in assets across Student Living (Scape), Rent to Live – Affordable Housing (RTL Co.), and Retirement Living (Aveo); spanning site origination, investment, planning, design, development, construction, and operations.\nThe Living Company is reshaping the way Australians live by delivering sustainable, community-driven, and high-quality spaces across the country.\nTHE ROLEAs FP&A Analyst within Group Commercial Finance, you'll support planning, forecasting and reporting across our student living, rent to live and retirement living platforms - owning much of the analytical layer beneath the group's management company numbers.\nDay-to-day you will be (but not limited to):\nPreparing and maintaining the group's revenue and management fee models, and supporting internal cost recharge and allocation calculations\nBuilding and maintaining annual budget and rolling forecast models, including reforecast cycles and scenario/sensitivity analysis\nSupporting monthly management reporting, variance analysis and commentary, and periodic flash reporting for executive decision-making\nBuilding and maintaining Power BI reports and dashboards, and the underlying data structures behind them\nActing as a finance contact for operational, corporate and investment teams, translating business plans into financial outcomes\nSimplifying and standardising spreadsheet models to keep them transparent, auditable and quick to review\nWHAT YOU'LL BRING\nDegree in Commerce, Finance, Accounting, Economics, Engineering or another quantitative discipline\n1-3 years in an FP&A, commercial finance or corporate finance role, or a first move into industry from a Big 4 or advisory background (transaction services, M&A, valuations or audit)\nCA or CPA qualified or progressing toward qualification (CFA equally relevant)\nAdvanced Excel and financial modelling skills, including Power Query and Power Pivot\nCompetence in Power BI, including data modelling, DAX and dashboard design (desired)\nPractical use of AI tools beyond basic chat - structured prompting, document/data extraction and building repeatable analytical workflows\nExposure to real estate, infrastructure or funds management, or experience with a major ERP platform (e.g. NetSuite, TechOne), will be highly regarded\nWHY SHOULD YOU JOIN?\nBe part of a purpose-led organisation shaping how Australians live\nExposure to a large, diversified living platform with real scale and complexity\nStrong focus on wellbeing, growth, and inclusive culture\nCompetitive rewards, recognition programs, and lifestyle benefits\nINTERESTED? HERE'S HOW TO APPLYIf this sounds like your next career move, we'd love to hear from you - apply now with your CV. Please note that we will be reviewing applications and contacting candidates on a rolling basis, so we encourage you to apply as early as possible.\nNo agencies please.\nAt The Living Company, we honour and welcome the rich heritage and contributions of First Nations and Indigenous peoples. Our workplace embraces diversity and strives to create an inclusive environment that respects and values your culture, traditions, and perspectives. Join us in building a harmonious and empowered community where everyone's voice is heard and celebrated.","source_board":"freehire:dayforce","source_external_id":"fp-a-analyst-scape-australia-go2bn3l3","source_url":"https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/scapeaus/internalportal/jobs/1303","source_posted_at":"2026-09-14T14:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"b56b13ca-8dcc-57f0-a217-dc93d38052fb","company_id":"6de52b2f-9a01-52d5-b1a2-cd2a6444fb9a","title":"FP&A Analyst","location":"Sydney, NSW, AU","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"1 years minimum","description":"Sydney CBD | Full-Time | On-Site (5 Days)\nWHO WE AREFounded in 2013 as Scape Australia, leaders in student housing, we've since grown into a vertically integrated living platform known as The Living Company; managing $18B in assets across Student Living (Scape), Rent to Live – Affordable Housing (RTL Co.), and Retirement Living (Aveo); spanning site origination, investment, planning, design, development, construction, and operations.\nThe Living Company is reshaping the way Australians live by delivering sustainable, community-driven, and high-quality spaces across the country.\nTHE ROLEAs FP&A Analyst within Group Commercial Finance, you'll support planning, forecasting and reporting across our student living, rent to live and retirement living platforms - owning much of the analytical layer beneath the group's management company numbers.\nDay-to-day you will be (but not limited to):\nPreparing and maintaining the group's revenue and management fee models, and supporting internal cost recharge and allocation calculations\nBuilding and maintaining annual budget and rolling forecast models, including reforecast cycles and scenario/sensitivity analysis\nSupporting monthly management reporting, variance analysis and commentary, and periodic flash reporting for executive decision-making\nBuilding and maintaining Power BI reports and dashboards, and the underlying data structures behind them\nActing as a finance contact for operational, corporate and investment teams, translating business plans into financial outcomes\nSimplifying and standardising spreadsheet models to keep them transparent, auditable and quick to review\nWHAT YOU'LL BRING\nDegree in Commerce, Finance, Accounting, Economics, Engineering or another quantitative discipline\n1-3 years in an FP&A, commercial finance or corporate finance role, or a first move into industry from a Big 4 or advisory background (transaction services, M&A, valuations or audit)\nCA or CPA qualified or progressing toward qualification (CFA equally relevant)\nAdvanced Excel and financial modelling skills, including Power Query and Power Pivot\nCompetence in Power BI, including data modelling, DAX and dashboard design (desired)\nPractical use of AI tools beyond basic chat - structured prompting, document/data extraction and building repeatable analytical workflows\nExposure to real estate, infrastructure or funds management, or experience with a major ERP platform (e.g. NetSuite, TechOne), will be highly regarded\nWHY SHOULD YOU JOIN?\nBe part of a purpose-led organisation shaping how Australians live\nExposure to a large, diversified living platform with real scale and complexity\nStrong focus on wellbeing, growth, and inclusive culture\nCompetitive rewards, recognition programs, and lifestyle benefits\nINTERESTED? HERE'S HOW TO APPLYIf this sounds like your next career move, we'd love to hear from you - apply now with your CV. Please note that we will be reviewing applications and contacting candidates on a rolling basis, so we encourage you to apply as early as possible.\nNo agencies please.\nAt The Living Company, we honour and welcome the rich heritage and contributions of First Nations and Indigenous peoples. Our workplace embraces diversity and strives to create an inclusive environment that respects and values your culture, traditions, and perspectives. Join us in building a harmonious and empowered community where everyone's voice is heard and celebrated.","source_board":"freehire:dayforce","source_external_id":"fp-a-analyst-the-living-company-uqy7ljar","source_url":"https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/scapeaus/thelivingcoccs/jobs/1301","source_posted_at":"2026-09-14T14:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"6ae13a1b-5b01-57f0-90da-6c585cd8cd82","company_id":"c9739e1d-6fce-5530-826f-3470f24af5bf","title":"FP&A Analyst, ANZ","location":"Rydalmere, NSW, AUSTRALIA","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"1 years minimum","description":"Hunter Douglas is the world’s leading manufacturer of window coverings and a major manufacturer of architectural products. We are a brand that you know and trust. With more than 100 years of innovation, we’ve defined our industry with proprietary products that deliver revolutionary style and functionality and can be found in millions of homes and commercial buildings globally.\n\nWe are searching for candidates that are driven, intelligent, creative, and entrepreneurial. By offering challenging and accelerated opportunities for growth, powered by a shared hunger for success, we create a space for your career to thrive. In return for your expertise, we are committed to providing competitive and robust total compensation and benefit packages to ensure you feel valued. Our dream is to become the fastest growing, most loved, window covering company in the world. What’s yours?\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe're looking for an analytical and commercially minded FP&A Analyst to join our ANZ Finance team. Reporting to the Head of FP&A & M&A – ANZ, you'll play a key role in supporting financial planning, reporting and commercial analysis across the business. This is an excellent opportunity for someone early in their FP&A career who is looking to broaden their experience, work closely with senior stakeholders, and contribute to strategic decision-making within a growing finance function.\n\nWhat You'll Be Doing\n\nAs our FP&A Analyst, you'll:\n\n• Support the annual budget, forecasting and long-range planning processes.\n\n• Prepare monthly management reports, financial analysis and performance insights.\n\n• Develop and maintain financial models, dashboards and forecasting tools.\n\n• Analyse revenue, costs, margins and key business drivers to support commercial decisions.\n\n• Assist with pricing, profitability and cost improvement initiatives.\n\n• Ensure financial data integrity and support governance and reporting standards.\n\n• Partner with stakeholders across the business to provide meaningful financial insights.\n\nAbout You\n\nYou'll be a motivated finance professional with strong analytical capability, a genuine interest in commercial finance, and a can-do attitude. You're someone who enjoys solving problems, takes ownership of your work, and thrives in a collaborative environment.\n\nYou'll bring:\n\n• A degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics or a related discipline.\n\n• 1–3 years' experience in FP&A, commercial finance, management accounting or public practice.\n\n• Advanced Microsoft Excel skills.\n\n• Strong analytical, critical thinking and problem-solving abilities with excellent attention to detail.\n\n• Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills.\n\n• A proactive approach, willingness to learn, and the ability to manage competing priorities.\n\nIt would be advantageous if you also have:\n\n• CA or CPA qualification (or are currently working towards it).\n\n• Experience working within a multinational organisation.\n\n• Exposure to BI, reporting or financial planning tools.\n\n• Manufacturing industry experience.\n\n• An interest in leveraging AI and technology to improve business processes.\n\nWhy Join Hunter Douglas?\n\nAt Hunter Douglas, you'll be part of a global market leader where innovation, collaboration and continuous improvement are at the heart of what we do. You'll have the opportunity to work alongside experienced finance professionals, develop your commercial acumen, and make a genuine impact on business performance across the ANZ region. We also offer:\n\n• Career growth: Access to structured development opportunities to support your professional advancement.\n\n• Employee benefits: Enjoy generous staff discounts on our premium products. \n\n• Birthday Leave: An extra day off in your birthday month!\n\n• Great culture: Be part of a supportive, collaborative team where your contribution makes an impact.\n\nIf you're looking to take the next step in your FP&A career, we'd love to hear from you.\n\nPlease note, all offers presented to candidates are carefully crafted to ensure market competitiveness, equity, and reflect the individual candidate’s education, experience, skills and potential.\n\n#Australia\n\nBy submitting your application below, you are providing your prior consent to receive SMS messages to notify you of any updates to your application status and to engage in discussion throughout your application process. You can cancel the SMS service at any time. Just text “STOP” to any of our texts to unsubscribe. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency may vary. If you have any questions regarding privacy, please read our privacy policy, or terms of use","source_board":"freehire:greenhouse","source_external_id":"fp-a-analyst-anz-hunterdouglas-mvfz66qq","source_url":"https://jobs.hunterdouglas.com/division/hunterdouglas/job/7786463003?gh_jid=7786463003","source_posted_at":"2026-09-11T10:26:52Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"9616fdde-5851-50fd-8dd4-5f3063a2a427","company_id":"874c564c-efe5-55ff-9d15-ed6f9e03c1ed","title":"Finance Analyst","location":"Sydney, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"2 years minimum","description":"Work Flexibility: Hybrid\n\nMake an impact where finance meets strategy.\nJoin Stryker’s Medical Asia Pacific (APAC) Finance team and play a key role in shaping business performance across the region. Reporting to the Commercial Manager, you will partner with senior leaders to provide financial insights, drive planning processes, and support decisions that improve growth, profitability, and operational performance.\nAs a trusted finance partner, you'll combine financial expertise, business intelligence, and commercial analysis to help leaders make informed decisions while contributing to continuous improvement initiatives across the business.\nWhat You Will Do\n\n• Lead the end-to-end forecasting, projection, and annual budgeting processes for the Medical APAC division.\n• Own monthly profit and loss reporting, ensuring financial results are accurate, complete, and delivered on time.\n• Analyze sales, margin, and operating performance to identify trends, risks, and opportunities that support business objectives.\n• Present monthly financial results, forecasts, and key business insights to regional leadership teams.\n• Partner with commercial leaders to evaluate business decisions, investments, and sales initiatives through financial analysis and performance modeling.\n• Provide actionable recommendations that improve revenue growth, profitability, and operational effectiveness.\n• Coordinate activities across accounting, compliance, taxation, and risk management functions to ensure alignment with corporate policies and regulatory requirements.\n• Deliver continuous improvement projects that enhance financial processes, reporting capabilities, and business outcomes.\n\nWhat You Will Need\nRequired Qualifications\n\n• Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Commerce, or a related discipline.\n• Minimum 2 years of experience in financial planning and analysis, commercial finance, management accounting, or a related finance role.\n• Experience preparing budgets, forecasts, management reports, and financial analyses.\n• Experience analyzing profit and loss statements and translating financial data into business recommendations.\n• Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and financial reporting tools.\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• Professional accounting qualification (CPA, CA, ACCA, or equivalent).\n• Experience supporting commercial, sales, or regional business operations within a multinational organization.\n• Experience participating in finance transformation or process improvement projects.\n\nAt Stryker, we are driven to improve healthcare outcomes through innovation, partnership, and performance. If you're passionate about using financial insights to influence business decisions and contribute to meaningful results, we'd love to hear from you.\n\nTravel Percentage: 10%","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"finance-analyst-stryker-uw3tjxnb","source_url":"https://stryker.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/StrykerCareers/job/Sydney-Australia/Finance-Analyst_R571675-1","source_posted_at":"2026-09-04T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"d7c04fe9-1c42-5c26-b454-42fba56d4c95","company_id":"f9b220a8-a4df-50cd-aa6b-5482497c0dac","title":"Junior Finance Analyst – Operations & Supply Chain","location":"Derrimut, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"1 years minimum","description":"Are you ready to scoop up an exciting career with one of Australia's most loved and trusted dairy brands? Bulla Dairy Foods is 100% Australian owned and operated and has been proudly making dairy products in country Australia for six generations. We are one of Australia's oldest family-owned dairy companies and believe in our brand, our people and take pride in crafting dairy products for the world.\n\nWe're looking for a Junior Finance Analyst to join our Commercial Finance team and play a key role in delivering financial reporting, analysis, and insights that support our Operations and Supply Chain teams. This is an excellent opportunity for someone with 1–2 years' post-qualification experience looking to develop their career in a collaborative and fast-paced environment. Working closely with Finance, Operations, Supply Chain, and IT stakeholders, you'll help identify key cost drivers, support budgeting and forecasting activities, and deliver meaningful insights that enable informed business decisions and drive operational performance.\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity for an ambitious finance professional looking to develop their analytical, business partnering, and commercial finance skills while gaining exposure to a diverse and fast-paced manufacturing environment.\n\nIf you're passionate about data, continuous improvement, and turning insights into action, we'd love to hear from you!\n\nWhat’s the Scoop?\n\n• Prepare monthly financial reporting, analysis, and commentary across Operations and Supply Chain.\n• Analyse key cost drivers including labour, waste, freight, warehousing, distribution, and manufacturing performance.\n• Support budgeting, forecasting, strategic planning, and financial performance reviews.\n• Develop and maintain reports, dashboards, and financial models to improve business insights and decision-making.\n• Partner with Finance, Operations, Supply Chain, Quality, and IT teams to improve reporting accuracy, data integrity, and process efficiency.\n• Track and report on continuous improvement, productivity, and cost-saving initiatives.\n• Assist with capital expenditure analysis, business cases, payback calculations, and post-implementation reviews.\n• Support S&OP reporting and provide financial insights to enhance operational and supply chain performance.\n• Contribute to ad hoc analysis, NPD initiatives, tenders, and strategic business projects.\n• Leverage AI and digital tools to improve reporting efficiency, analytical capability, and insight generation while maintaining strong data governance.\n\nWhat You’ll Bring:\n\nWe're looking for someone who is analytical, curious and keen to learn.\n\n• A tertiary qualification in Accounting, Finance, Commerce or a related discipline.\n• Approximately 1–2 years' experience in finance, accounting or financial analysis\n• Strong Excel skills with the ability to analyse and interpret data.\n• Excellent attention to detail and problem-solving skills.\n• Strong communication skills and the confidence to work with stakeholders across the business.\n• A desire to continue developing your commercial finance career (CA/CPA studies commenced or willingness to undertake them is highly regarded).\n• Experience within manufacturing, supply chain or FMCG is advantageous but not essential.\n\nWhy Bulla?\n\nAt Bulla, we’re not just about ice cream – we’re about creating a culture that’s as rich and satisfying as our creamy classics. Here’s what we offer:\n\n• Hybrid Work Model - Flexibility to work from home and the office \n• Parental Leave - Inclusive Options for all caregiver types, with flexible return-to-work support\n• Learning & Development – Career pathways, mentoring and training and graduate programs \n• Wellbeing Support – Flu shots, and 24/7 mental health services\n• Fun Culture – Team BBQs, celebrations, and festive events\n• Diverse & Inclusive Environment – A safe, supportive workplace for all\n• Competitive Pay & Perks – Annual reviews, bonuses, and salary packaging\n• Novated Leasing – Exclusive discounts on corporate fleet vehicles\n• Corporate Uniform Allowance – Stylish uniform allowance and staff discounts from an iconic Australian brand\n• Office Perks – Free fruit, coffee, and Bulla treats at work\n• Volunteer Leave – One paid day each year to give back\n• Transparent Communication – Stay engaged with regular updates and events\n• Convenient Locations – Multiple sites across Victoria with free parking\n\nReady to Join the Bulla Family?\n\nThis is a rare and exciting opportunity within a reputable family business. With great opportunities for personal growth and development, you'll contribute to the success of this iconic household brand with a long history and bright future. \n\nApply now by “hitting apply” to join the Bulla family. \n\nAt Bulla Dairy Foods, we are dedicated to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive culture where everyone feels they belong. We value diversity and the unique contributions of each team member. Our goal is to create an environment where all employees feel valued, respected, and safe, enabling them to perform at their best and reach their potential","source_board":"freehire:breezy","source_external_id":"junior-finance-analyst-operations-supply-chain-bulla-dairy-foods-6xkykhtl","source_url":"https://bulla.breezy.hr/p/9445ef7682ed-junior-finance-analyst-operations-supply-chain","source_posted_at":"2026-08-22T14:14:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"c2967161-5897-57cf-bad9-1d1e90152279","company_id":"60a05983-7c12-5b48-a932-52698cb2c5e4","title":"Business Finance Analyst, Financial Planning and Analysis","location":"Sydney NSW, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"2 years minimum","description":"Financial Analysts ensure that Google makes sound financial decisions. As a Financial Analyst, your work, whether it's modeling business scenarios or tracking performance metrics, is used by our leaders to make strategic company decisions. While working on multiple projects at a time, you are focused on the details while finding creative ways to solve big picture challenges.\n\nThe name Google came from \"googol,\" a mathematical term for the number 1 followed by 100 zeros. And nobody at Google loves big numbers like the Finance team when providing in depth analysis on all manner of strategic decisions across Google products. From developing forward-thinking analysis to generating management reports to scaling our automated financial processes, the Finance organization is an important partner and advisor to the business.\n\n• Perform in-depth financial analyses to identify growth drivers to influence business activity. Provide management with clear insights and recommendations into the business, market trends, risks and opportunities leading to business enhancement and sales actions, collaborating with other finance analysts.\n\n• Maintain data pipelines and dashboards using SQL and internal sales tools (e.g. connect sales) to deliver accurate insights, and assist in automating manual reporting processes using AI tools.\n\n• Drive efficiency and accuracy in critical finance processes including weekly trading reviews, revenue forecasting and quota setting.\n\nMinimum qualifications:\n\n• Bachelor's degree or equivalent practical experience.\n\n• 2 years of experience in investment banking, corporate finance and management consulting.\n\n• Experience in analytics, spreadsheets, SQL, and working with data.\n\nPreferred qualifications:\n\n• Experience working within or supporting sales organizations, in the technology or advertising industry.","source_board":"freehire:google","source_external_id":"business-finance-analyst-financial-planning-and-analysis-google-mkqwz7g4","source_url":"https://www.google.com/about/careers/applications/jobs/results/136750612539679430","source_posted_at":"2026-08-19T07:44:36Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"142fe589-6987-5ec5-9ab8-7577485bf932","company_id":"4f49282a-b221-5115-98de-3dc37d94e598","title":"FP&A Analyst","location":"Yatala, Queensland, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"3 years minimum","description":"• The FP & A Analyst is responsible for gathering and analyzing financial data as well as for creating and maintaining financial and resource reports and presentations. This role will perform budget tracking, variance and trend analysis, support with financial forecasting, resource reporting and evaluation monitoring for in-flight initiatives. Responsible for compiling and maintaining data and support documentation for compliance and audit reviews.\n\n• Responsible for budget tracking, financial variance and trend analysis, support to financial forecasting, resource reporting and evaluation monitoring.\n• Build reports for operational teams using current tools interpreting and guiding operations management requirements.\n• Responsible for compiling and maintaining data and support documentation for compliance and audit reviews.\n• Provide financial analysis with a focus on price dynamics within the company’s businesses.\n• Prepare and summarize operational reports and help generate and monitor sales forecasts.\n• Develop financial reports for forecasting, trending, and results analysis.\n• Manage difficult analytical projects with limited supervision.\n• Perform research on industry statistics, competition, and other trends that affect the industry\n• Work closely with the management teams to provide decision critical information and reports.\n• Perform other duties as assigned.\n\n• 3+ years of experience in financial analysis, project management administration, cost controlling or monitoring and reporting\n• Ability to communicate effectively at all levels.\n• Ability to plan and prioritize workload.\n• Extremely detail-oriented and organized","source_board":"freehire:oracle","source_external_id":"fp-a-analyst-ritchie-bros-vdw7frcx","source_url":"https://fa-exew-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/jobsearch/job/9911","source_posted_at":"2026-05-20T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"c5730b0b-287f-5af6-aad7-34ed51224b20","company_id":"20a76095-ae82-5918-a49f-66219ee5d4b0","title":"FP&A Analyst","location":"Yatala, Queensland, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"3 years minimum","description":"• The FP & A Analyst is responsible for gathering and analyzing financial data as well as for creating and maintaining financial and resource reports and presentations. This role will perform budget tracking, variance and trend analysis, support with financial forecasting, resource reporting and evaluation monitoring for in-flight initiatives. Responsible for compiling and maintaining data and support documentation for compliance and audit reviews.\n\n• Responsible for budget tracking, financial variance and trend analysis, support to financial forecasting, resource reporting and evaluation monitoring.\n• Build reports for operational teams using current tools interpreting and guiding operations management requirements.\n• Responsible for compiling and maintaining data and support documentation for compliance and audit reviews.\n• Provide financial analysis with a focus on price dynamics within the company’s businesses.\n• Prepare and summarize operational reports and help generate and monitor sales forecasts.\n• Develop financial reports for forecasting, trending, and results analysis.\n• Manage difficult analytical projects with limited supervision.\n• Perform research on industry statistics, competition, and other trends that affect the industry\n• Work closely with the management teams to provide decision critical information and reports.\n• Perform other duties as assigned.\n\n• 3+ years of experience in financial analysis, project management administration, cost controlling or monitoring and reporting\n• Ability to communicate effectively at all levels.\n• Ability to plan and prioritize workload.\n• Extremely detail-oriented and organized","source_board":"freehire:oracle","source_external_id":"fp-a-analyst-rbglobal-6ovea27m","source_url":"https://fa-exew-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/9911","source_posted_at":"2026-05-20T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"1bdb96a8-6143-5ed0-8f1c-2e838db90917","company_id":"5463774b-04de-50b2-a223-e112e66d1888","title":"Associate Financial Analyst (Capital Planning & Reporting)","location":"Carlton, Kogarah Area","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"entry-level title","description":"JD excerpt from adzuna; read the complete posting at https://www.adzuna.com.au/land/ad/5888740343?se=jvMvmPCz8RGSI57gYuD12g&v=2FC6F132A3769D783D21FC5BD3E07BAA5B6FDCA8\n\nExpected Salary Range: $65941 - $82426 Annually The salary range shown above reflects the expected compensation for this position. The final salary offered will be determined based on a holistic assessment of the candidate’s experience, education, training, and alignment with the role’s requirements. For positions covered by a collective agreement, placement within the range will follow the applicable step or classification. Reporting to the Manager, Capital Planning & Reporting; the Associate …","source_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5888740343","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/land/ad/5888740343?se=jvMvmPCz8RGSI57gYuD12g&v=2FC6F132A3769D783D21FC5BD3E07BAA5B6FDCA8","source_posted_at":"2026-09-18T15:18:08Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"fin