upport business-process improvement, JDE Finance configuration, system enhancement and implementation activity. The role · Work with Finance and IT teams to design and implement improvements to the JD Edwards Finance model. · Support and lead JDE rollout activity for newly ac…","source_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5848076254","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5848076254","source_posted_at":"2026-08-19T20:40:41Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"1ed9ee19-8e36-5371-bb16-dd6765e21630","company_id":"acf341d2-97f0-5271-8098-470c313317cd","title":"Commercial Analyst/Associate","location":"Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"entry-level title","description":"JD excerpt from adzuna; read the complete posting at https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5788631324\n\nDescription Role Purpose: The Commercial Analyst/Associate plays a critical role within an Equis-controlled platform, supporting commercial execution, transaction delivery, and asset management activities across the energy transition portfolio. The role combines financial modelling, commercial analysis, and hands-on transaction support across assets from development through construction and into operations. The Commercial Analyst/Associate works closely with senior leadership to ensure assets a…","source_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5788631324","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5788631324","source_posted_at":"2026-07-05T11:06:59Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"f36206d0-026a-5883-9308-4599400f64ee","company_id":"ca6b2a93-5c6d-52af-8e84-5d90034613d0","title":"GSK 12 Month Internship - Finance Analyst","location":"Abbotsford, Yarra Area","job_type":"internship","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"entry-level title","description":"JD excerpt from adzuna; read the complete posting at https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5753220279\n\nBack GSK 12 Month Internship - Finance Analyst JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML Abbotsford, Australia Administrative Services mail_outline Get future jobs matching this search LoginorRegister Job description Site Name: Australia - Victoria - Abbotsford Posted Date: Jun 4 2026 About the Role Are you currently in your penultimate or final year of undergraduate studies in a bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting or a related field at university and ready …","source_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5753220279","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5753220279","source_posted_at":"2026-06-05T22:55:40Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"d4689ca7-1bf6-58fc-a40c-92ef278af15c","company_id":"89a99d6a-ed6d-5aa8-b843-a2016c0efae0","title":"Corporate Finance / Equity Capital Markets - Associate or Analyst","location":"The Rocks, Sydney","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"entry-level title","description":"JD excerpt from adzuna; read the complete posting at https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5650819612\n\nSydney Investment Banking Permanent Our client is a leading institutional equities broking and advisory firm seeking an experienced ECM / Corporate Finance Associate or Analyst reporting into the Head of Corporate. We are seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented professional to join our client’s Corporate Finance team, with a primary focus on equity capital markets (ECM) , including IPOs, pre-IPO transactions, and secondary market capital raisings (on-market placements, rights issues, and…","source_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5650819612","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5650819612","source_posted_at":"2026-03-02T14:41:22Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"1253ca70-f444-5010-9192-84953b9cf6d9","company_id":"e0894684-0270-5393-81b3-2a64e73bfef8","title":"Commercial Finance Analyst","location":"Melbourne, VIC","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"At Saputo, we bring good to the table by making high-quality products, investing in our people, and supporting communities around the world . As a top 10 global dairy processor, we value contributions that matter and strive to foster an inclusive, growth-driven work environment. Ready to bring your best?\n\nHow you will make contributions that matter\n\nJoin Saputo Dairy Australia as a Commercial Analyst within our FP&A team at Freshwater Place. This role combines accurate commercial reporting with analysis, curiosity and business partnering. You will bring together financial information, investigate the story behind the numbers and provide insights that support better decisions across finance and the broader business. Key elements of your role will include:\n\n• Preparing daily and weekly sales reports for Foodservices and Route channels\n• Consolidating weekly Commercial P&L reporting and providing clear commentary\n• Completing month-end reconciliations, journals and profitability reporting\n• Supporting budgeting, forecasting and division-wide management reporting\n• Analysing customer profitability, purchase price variance, freight and inventory\n• Partnering with Commercial Finance, Sales, Operations, Procurement and site finance to understand performance drivers\n• Investigating trends and anomalies, identifying issues and turning data into practical commercial insights\n• Contributing to regular and ad hoc business performance analysis and projects\n\nAbout you\n\n• Tertiary qualification in Business, Finance or Accounting, together with a CA or CPA qualification\n• At least three years’ relevant experience, ideally within FMCG, manufacturing, dairy or another complex commercial environment\n• Advanced Excel capability, including building, running and interpreting financial reports and models\n• Strong analytical skills and genuine curiosity to understand what is driving the numbers\n• Sound commercial acumen and the confidence to provide meaningful commentary and recommendations\n• High attention to detail, strong organisation and the ability to deliver accurate work to agreed timeframes\n• A proactive, hands-on and self-directed approach, with the willingness to seek answers rather than wait for direction\n• Clear communication skills and the ability to build relationships and influence stakeholders\n• Experience with BI reporting tools; SAP exposure is advantageous but not essential\n\nWe’ll support you with\n\n• The opportunity to make contributions that matter, whilst being supported by a multinational, values-led company\n• A competitive annual salary\n• Learning and development opportunities with the ability to grow in your own way\n• The ability to participate in our Employee Share Ownership Program\n\nClick on Apply for this job to submit your application.\nSaputo Dairy Australia is an equal opportunity employer. All applicants require Australian working rights at the time of applying. \n\nAs a leading dairy processor in Australia, Saputo produces, markets, and distributes a variety of products, with a portfolio of well-loved brands such as Devondale, Liddells, CHEER, Mersey Valley and Tasmanian Heritage. Our people bring these popular brands to life, while servicing our farming communities and through our AG Warehouse network. \n\nWhether your expertise lies in manufacturing, operations, supply chain, sales, quality assurance, or in any other function, your role is integral to our success. You will make contributions that matter, all while working alongside colleagues who genuinely care about your success and who will roll up their sleeves to help.","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"commercial-finance-analyst-saputo-a5yk6i7y","source_url":"https://saputo.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Saputo_External_Careers/job/Melbourne-VIC/Commercial-Finance-Analyst_JR66826","source_posted_at":"2026-09-18T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"497c5556-cb69-558e-9f6f-2d446beb77e7","company_id":"f460eb38-59b8-5487-aac4-dcc0bf760e89","title":"Finance Business Analyst - Banking, Payments & Accounting","location":"Melbourne VIC","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"We are seeking an experienced Finance Business Analyst to support a significant finance transformation initiative.\n\nThis role is suited to a commercially minded Business Analyst who can speak the language of finance and work confidently with accountants, finance leaders, banking partners, payment teams and technology stakeholders. \n\nThe successful candidate does not need to be deeply technical but must possess a strong understanding of finance, accounting, banking and payment processes.\n\nExperience with Oracle NetSuite would be highly regarded.\n\nKey Responsibilities \n\n• Analyse and document current finance, accounting, banking and payment processes. \n• Gather business requirements from finance, treasury, accounts payable, accounts receivable and operational stakeholders. \n• Map end-to-end financial processes, including payments, receipts, settlements, reconciliations and reporting. \n• Translate finance requirements into clear business requirements, process maps, user stories and acceptance criteria. \n• Identify process gaps, control weaknesses, inefficiencies and opportunities for improvement. \n• Support the design of future-state finance and accounting processes. \n• Work with finance teams and delivery partners to define system and reporting requirements. \n• Analyse banking interfaces, payment flows, transaction data and reconciliation processes. \n• Support data mapping, migration, validation and financial system integration activities. \n• Facilitate workshops and maintain alignment between finance, business and technology stakeholders. \n• Assist with testing, defect management, implementation, training and business readiness. \n• Ensure proposed solutions support appropriate financial controls, auditability and reporting obligations. Required Experience \n\n• Strong experience as a Business Analyst working across finance or accounting transformation programs. \n• Sound knowledge of accounting principles and core financial processes. \n• Experience with banking, payments, settlements and financial reconciliations. \n• Ability to communicate effectively with accountants, finance executives and operational stakeholders. \n• Experience documenting complex finance processes and business requirements. \n• Strong analytical, process-mapping and problem-solving capabilities. \n• Experience supporting system implementations, process improvements or finance transformation initiatives. \n• Excellent workshop facilitation, stakeholder-management and communication skills. Highly Desirable \n\n• Experience with Oracle NetSuite. \n• Experience implementing or enhancing an ERP or finance platform. \n• Knowledge of general ledger, accounts payable, accounts receivable, cash management and financial reporting. \n• Experience with banking integrations, payment gateways or payment service providers. \n• Exposure to retail or other high-volume transactional environments. The successful candidate will be finance and accounting savvy, comfortable discussing banking and payment processes, and capable of bridging the gap between finance stakeholders and delivery teams.\n\nApply now or contact Milestone IT on (0) 9670 6682 for a confidential discussion.","source_board":"freehire:seek","source_external_id":"finance-business-analyst-banking-payments-accounting-milestone-information-technology-n445r4eh","source_url":"https://www.seek.com.au/job/94700729","source_posted_at":"2026-09-17T07:28:12Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"7aa105ef-7d2b-57de-bdec-938bad9e71a1","company_id":"6d1e454a-7319-5a2f-bcea-a561a59a4c83","title":"Commercial Finance Analyst - DC Australia","location":"Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"ABOUT US\nRetail is in our DNA and at Cotton On, we believe every part of our business plays a role in delivering an exceptional customer experience. \nOur Avalon DC is where the scale of our business comes to life. It’s our largest global distribution centre - 50,000 sqm, 1,000 team members, and the critical link between our product and our customers across 700 stores and 8 brands.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE \n\nWe’re looking for a high-performing Commercial Finance Analyst to support our Distribution and Freight teams on a 12 month fixed term contract. This is a role for someone who’s not just good with numbers, but passionate about turning complex data into simple, intelligent insights that influence commercial decisions.\nYou’ll work closely with the Commercial Finance Manager and Heads of Country Distribution with preparation of annual budgets, monthly reporting and forecasting, building robust financial models, automating reporting and crafting visual, high quality outputs that tell a clear story. You thrive in Excel, love working at pace, and have a sharp eye for both detail and the bigger picture.\nYou love solving problems, not just crunching numbers but working across functions to understand the context, ask the right questions, and land on solutions that truly add value. Your curiosity and commercial mindset are what will set you up for success in this role.\nYou bring strong communication skills, can translate financial information for non-finance stakeholders, and take pride in producing high-quality, presentation-ready outputs. If you're someone who loves making data meaningful and wants to help shape the performance of our Supply Chain, we’d love to hear from you.\n\nSKILLS & EXPERIENCE\n\n• Experience in a similar Commercial Finance Analyst role including budgeting and forecasting\n• Experience in the month end process and the ability to raise accruals and adjustments where required\n• CA or CPA qualified, or studying towards, would be highly regarded\n• A naturally analytical and curious mindset, with strong critical thinking skills \n• Advanced Microsoft Excel skills. You can confidently build models, manipulate large data sets, automate and simplify \n• Experience (or strong capability) in visualising data and presenting it in a clear way \n• The ability to simplify complex data into meaningful insights for both finance and non-finance stakeholders \n• A proactive, solutions-focused approach, always looking for better, faster, smarter ways to work \n• High attention to detail, with a commitment to accuracy \n• Strong communication skills\n\nOUR CULTURE\nNo fuss, no worries, we’ll roll up our sleeves and make it happen. But we go beyond just ‘doing the right thing’; we work in local communities and support them however we can.\nWhile we’re working hard today, our eyes are always on tomorrow. Together we help to make tomorrow a better place for our stores, customers, work mates and each other.\n\nBENEFITS \n\nCompetitive wage\n50% team member discount off all brands (excl. Ceres Life which is 30% off)\nSafe working environment\nWe genuinely care about our people. It’s more than just a job to us.\n\nAt Cotton On, we are focused on building a culture centred in belonging, and we are committed to creating workplaces where each individual can show up as their whole self, having an equal opportunity to succeed with us.\nWe are proud of our diverse global workforce of 20,000 team members from countless nationalities, and we strongly welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to apply with us.\nWe are focused on bringing more voices, experiences and backgrounds to our workforce as we drive diverse and inclusive outcomes for our team and our customers. \n\nIf you have any individual needs in order to fully participate in the recruitment process, please contact us at recruitment@cottonon.com.au so we may support you in completing the job application process.","source_board":"freehire:oracle","source_external_id":"commercial-finance-analyst-dc-australia-cotton-on-group-sfq6q6y7","source_url":"https://ekxm.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/jobsearch/job/58493","source_posted_at":"2026-09-16T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"a9d65204-97eb-50cf-ac91-2452a6063d61","company_id":"f9ab1ff4-8241-5225-bda0-47b85659c9bf","title":"Financial Analyst - Cash and Working Capital","location":"North Ryde, NSW, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"The opportunity\nAs a Financial Analyst – Working Capital & Cash, you will support the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of cash and working capital reporting, forecasting, and controls across the Energy & Utilities business. \n\nWorking closely with finance teams, treasury, shared services, and operational stakeholders, you will provide valuable insights that help optimise cash performance and support strategic decision-making.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\n• Deliver daily, weekly, and monthly cash, working capital, and CAPEX reporting, forecasting, and analysis.\n• Monitor cash inflows, outflows, debtor balances, work in progress, and other key working capital metrics across multiple business units and contracts.\n• Partner with business unit finance teams to identify trends, risks, and opportunities and improve cash management practices.\n• Support treasury reporting requirements, including 12-week cash forecasts and participation in weekly cash review processes.\n• Drive continuous improvement initiatives by developing reporting tools, controls, and analytical solutions that improve data quality, efficiency, and business performance.\n\nWhat we offer\n\n• Opportunity to contribute to a high-performing finance function within a large and complex business.\n• Exposure to working capital management, treasury processes, forecasting, and commercial finance activities.\n• Collaborative environment where you can build relationships across finance, operations, treasury, and shared services teams.\n• Ongoing opportunities to develop your technical, analytical, and commercial skills.\n\nWhat we’re looking for\n\n• Tertiary qualification in Accounting, Commerce, or a related discipline.\n• Experience in accounting, treasury, business analysis, or commercial finance within a medium to large organisation.\n• Strong analytical capability with advanced Excel skills and experience working with ERP and reporting systems.\n• Ability to interpret large volumes of financial and transactional data and translate findings into meaningful business insights.\n• Excellent stakeholder engagement, communication, relationship-building, and problem-solving skills.\n\nDesirable\n\n• Working towards or holding a CA, CPA, or equivalent qualification.\n• Experience with cash flow, working capital, or CAPEX reporting and forecasting.\n\nAbout Energy & Utilities\nDowner’s Energy & Utilities business delivers integrated services across the utility lifecycle, supporting customers in the design, construction, maintenance, and operation of critical infrastructure. Our teams work together to deliver safe, reliable, and sustainable outcomes for the communities we serve.\n\nHow to apply\nIf you're a proactive and commercially focused finance professional looking to make an impact through cash and working capital performance, we'd love to hear from you. Submit your application online and include a current resume outlining your experience and suitability for the role.","source_board":"freehire:oracle","source_external_id":"financial-analyst-cash-and-working-capital-downer-pgim4ai5","source_url":"https://fa-exfs-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/jobsearch/job/736671","source_posted_at":"2026-09-16T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"7eba600a-b23c-58d4-8383-1fa5d31908c9","company_id":"2d4d7269-37ad-5dde-b69a-aea1c98b2efb","title":"Commercial Finance Analyst - DC Australia","location":"Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"ABOUT US\nRetail is in our DNA and at Cotton On, we believe every part of our business plays a role in delivering an exceptional customer experience. \nOur Avalon DC is where the scale of our business comes to life. It’s our largest global distribution centre - 50,000 sqm, 1,000 team members, and the critical link between our product and our customers across 700 stores and 8 brands.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE \n\nWe’re looking for a high-performing Commercial Finance Analyst to support our Distribution and Freight teams on a 12 month fixed term contract. This is a role for someone who’s not just good with numbers, but passionate about turning complex data into simple, intelligent insights that influence commercial decisions.\nYou’ll work closely with the Commercial Finance Manager and Heads of Country Distribution with preparation of annual budgets, monthly reporting and forecasting, building robust financial models, automating reporting and crafting visual, high quality outputs that tell a clear story. You thrive in Excel, love working at pace, and have a sharp eye for both detail and the bigger picture.\nYou love solving problems, not just crunching numbers but working across functions to understand the context, ask the right questions, and land on solutions that truly add value. Your curiosity and commercial mindset are what will set you up for success in this role.\nYou bring strong communication skills, can translate financial information for non-finance stakeholders, and take pride in producing high-quality, presentation-ready outputs. If you're someone who loves making data meaningful and wants to help shape the performance of our Supply Chain, we’d love to hear from you.\n\nSKILLS & EXPERIENCE\n\n• Experience in a similar Commercial Finance Analyst role including budgeting and forecasting\n• Experience in the month end process and the ability to raise accruals and adjustments where required\n• CA or CPA qualified, or studying towards, would be highly regarded\n• A naturally analytical and curious mindset, with strong critical thinking skills \n• Advanced Microsoft Excel skills. You can confidently build models, manipulate large data sets, automate and simplify \n• Experience (or strong capability) in visualising data and presenting it in a clear way \n• The ability to simplify complex data into meaningful insights for both finance and non-finance stakeholders \n• A proactive, solutions-focused approach, always looking for better, faster, smarter ways to work \n• High attention to detail, with a commitment to accuracy \n• Strong communication skills\n\nOUR CULTURE\nNo fuss, no worries, we’ll roll up our sleeves and make it happen. But we go beyond just ‘doing the right thing’; we work in local communities and support them however we can.\nWhile we’re working hard today, our eyes are always on tomorrow. Together we help to make tomorrow a better place for our stores, customers, work mates and each other.\n\nBENEFITS \n\nCompetitive wage\n50% team member discount off all brands (excl. Ceres Life which is 30% off)\nSafe working environment\nWe genuinely care about our people. It’s more than just a job to us.\n\nAt Cotton On, we are focused on building a culture centred in belonging, and we are committed to creating workplaces where each individual can show up as their whole self, having an equal opportunity to succeed with us.\nWe are proud of our diverse global workforce of 20,000 team members from countless nationalities, and we strongly welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to apply with us.\nWe are focused on bringing more voices, experiences and backgrounds to our workforce as we drive diverse and inclusive outcomes for our team and our customers. \n\nIf you have any individual needs in order to fully participate in the recruitment process, please contact us at recruitment@cottonon.com.au so we may support you in completing the job application process.","source_board":"freehire:oracle","source_external_id":"commercial-finance-analyst-dc-australia-cotton-on-4tveriyt","source_url":"https://ekxm.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/58493","source_posted_at":"2026-09-16T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"ffa3c486-fcba-57e9-9b29-5a6b7989c147","company_id":"83135fae-d8c1-5e6e-ab04-ab4b360979f6","title":"Financial Analyst","location":"Fortitude Valley, Queensland","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"At Urban Utilities, our purpose is simple yet powerful – Enrich Quality of Life. With a $7 billion asset base and services spanning 1.5 million residents and more than 31,000 commercial customers across South East Queensland, we are committed to enhancing the liveability of our communities every day.\n\nYour opportunity:\n\nAs a Financial Analyst, you’ll play a key role in supporting financial planning, performance reporting, and analysis that helps drive informed business decisions across Urban Utilities. Working within the Enterprise Performance team, you’ll provide valuable insights that contribute to improved operational and financial outcomes.\n\nIn this varied role, you’ll assist with the preparation of budgets, forecasts, and periodic performance reports, helping leaders understand business performance and progress against strategic and operational objectives. You’ll develop and maintain financial models, databases, and reporting tools, providing timely analysis and insights that support effective decision-making.\n\nPartnering closely with stakeholders across the business, you’ll build trusted relationships and contribute to a culture of continuous improvement. You'll have the opportunity to identify smarter ways of working, leveraging digital tools and automation to enhance reporting, streamline processes, and deliver a seamless experience for both employees and the business.\n\nAbout you:\n\nYou're a commercially minded finance professional who enjoys transforming complex data into meaningful insights that drive business performance. You have strong analytical and financial modelling capabilities, thrive in a collaborative environment, and can confidently communicate financial information to a variety of stakeholders.\n\nTo be successful in this role, you will bring:\n\n• \nExperience developing and maintaining complex financial models to support forecasting, scenario analysis, and business sustainability planning.\n• \nStrong analytical skills, with the ability to interpret financial and operational data, identify trends, and assess risks and opportunities.\n• \nExperience conducting variance analysis, reviewing actual performance against budgets and forecasts, and providing recommendations to support data-driven decision-making.\n• \nDemonstrated involvement in budgeting, forecasting, and annual planning processes, including gathering inputs and supporting the preparation of executive-level reporting.\n• \nKnowledge of month-end financial processes, including accruals, prepayments, cost allocations, and financial reporting activities.\n• \nThe ability to prepare clear, accurate, and insightful reports that connect financial and operational performance and tell a compelling story through data.\n• \nStrong stakeholder engagement and relationship-building skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across business units and support leaders with meaningful financial insights.\n\nAt Urban Utilities, we believe our workforce should reflect the community we serve. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and experiences, including First Nations peoples, people with disability, members of the LGBTIQ+ community, veterans, emergency responders and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds.\nYou might not meet every single requirement listed. If you are excited about the role and believe you can make a strong contribution, we encourage you to apply.\n\nIf you require adjustments at any stage of the recruitment process, please let us know so we can support you.\n\nWhy Urban Utilities\n\nUrban Utilities delivers essential water and wastewater services to more than 1.5 million people across Southeast Queensland. Every day, our teams work to support thriving communities and a sustainable future.\n\n• \nGenerous Salary Packaging options, including novated leases\n• \nCorporate discounts across Health insurance, technology and more\n• \n18 weeks of paid parental leave, 15 days personal leave including two proactive wellbeing days, and an additional day of leave each year to connect with friends and family\n• \nFlexibility at UU depends on the type of work you do but could include options such as, 9-day fortnights and flexible days. Talk to us about what flexibility means to you!\n• \nUrban Utilities is an endorsed employer for all women. See our range of benefits and policies directly at WORK180\n\nThere’s no us without you. Come shape the future with us.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nClick ‘Apply’ to submit your application.\n\nPlease note: applicants may be required to undergo a Pre-employment medical, which may include Drug and Alcohol testing, as well as other background checks as part of the recruitment process for this role.\n\nFor further information please contact our Talent team at careers@urbanutilities.com.au\n\nOur Talent team & Hiring Managers kindly request that no unsolicited CVs are sent for this role.","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"financial-analyst-urban-utilities-j5hgiusc","source_url":"https://urbanutilities.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UrbanCareers/job/Fortitude-Valley-Queensland/Financial-Analyst_R3907-2","source_posted_at":"2026-09-16T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"92ab082d-8657-519e-8d0c-d3dd7b56bcf6","company_id":"fd4a79be-181d-5ac0-8d5a-6b7d88ce9a26","title":"Finance Analyst","location":"Australia (Flexible)","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"Employment TypePermanent\n\nClosing Date26 Sept 2026 11:59pm\n\nJob TitleFinance Analyst\n\nJob Summary\nJob Description\nWe’ve adopted an Agile way of working to better prioritise the work that matters, match the right resources to the right work, and support our people’s development. It helps us move faster, stay aligned, and deliver more value to our business stakeholders, customers and shareholders.\n\nThis role sits within the Financial Management Chapter Area, a global team of around 400 finance professionals who partner with the business to deliver financial insight, strategic decision support and performance management across the organisation.\n\nThe role with us\nAs a Finance Analyst within our Financial Management Chapter Area, you will play a critical role delivering insight and driving change via our Agile way of working. While your role will vary from mission to mission, the capabilities and scope of our finance analysts do not.\n\nOur Finance Analysts combine business partnering, financial management and analytical capability to help leaders make informed decisions. This includes financial planning, forecasting, performance reporting, commercial analysis, accounting support and strategic advice.\nWe support more than 40 missions across Telstra, creating opportunities to apply your skills in a wide range of business contexts while building broad commercial and finance experience.\n\nThis is how you'll bring the purpose of your role to life:\n\n• \nSupport month-end, forecasting and financial control activities, ensuring accurate, timely and high-quality financial outcomes through effective P&L management, reporting and analysis.\n• \nUse financial analysis, modelling and data-driven insights to evaluate performance, identify key business drivers, and uncover risks and opportunities.\n• \nProvide commercial insights and recommendations that support business cases, investment decisions and strategic initiatives.\n• \nBuild trusted relationships with stakeholders, providing financial insight that supports strategic priorities and better business outcomes.\n• \nOwn your work and contribute independently to management reporting and financial results for assigned business areas.\n• \nContinuously interrogate your work to ensure it adds value, automate where possible, eliminate low-impact tasks, and seek smarter ways of working.\n• \nBring a continuous improvement mindset to forecasting and planning, using best-practice approaches to enhance models and processes.\n• \nBuild subject matter expertise and stay across trends impacting financial and operational performance.\n\nTo be successful in the role, you should have:\n\n• \nCA or CPA qualification\n• \nExperience in accounting, audit, financial reporting, FP&A, management accounting or finance business partnering.\n• \nStrong accounting fundamentals, including financial reporting, balance sheet management, financial controls and financial analysis.\n• \nStrong analytical skills with high attention to detail and the ability to translate financial data into meaningful business insights.\n• \nA growth mindset, strong problem-solving skills and the confidence to challenge assumptions and seek better ways of working.\n• \nExcellent stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to influence and partner effectively across the business.\n• \nA genuine interest in improving business performance through financial insight and commercial thinking \n\nHighly regarded:\n\n• \nExperience within a Big 4 or mid-tier professional services environment.\n• \nExperience in a large, complex corporate organisation.\n• \nAdvanced Excel and financial modelling capabilities.\nIf you are dedicated to developing yourself, have a desire to always achieve more then we want to hear from you! Above all, you will bring enthusiasm and dedication to your job, are not afraid of hard work, and thrive off the satisfaction gained from achieving success in addressing and successfully overcoming challenges.\n\nTelstra is an equal opportunity employer and we value diversity. We’re also committed to flexibility and open to considering flexible ways of working for every role.","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"finance-analyst-telastra-2j2e2dba","source_url":"https://telstra.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Telstra_Careers/job/Australia-Flexible/Finance-Analyst_JR-10175274-1","source_posted_at":"2026-09-15T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"0d62a539-10c6-5257-ae33-b3fc898dc2de","company_id":"88457c9d-936c-5a54-8a90-0787962e000d","title":"Finance Analyst","location":"Mitcham, VIC, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"ABOUT US\n\nThe Salvation Army is a Christian movement and one of Australia's largest and most-loved charities. We believe in doing good that transforms lives and futures for the better. It is this belief which drives us to find new ways and places where we can make a difference. From times of personal crisis to moments of national grief, we are always here — providing support, safety, community, and opportunity.\n\nAbout the Role\nWe are seeking a Finance Analyst for a permanent, full-time opportunity to join our Finance team in Melbourne. Working closely with Finance Business Partner and operational leaders, you will provide data-driven insights, predictive analysis, and commercial support to help drive informed decision-making and improve business performance. Your work will contribute to better financial outcomes while supporting The Salvation Army's mission and strategic objectives.\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity for someone who enjoys turning data into meaningful insights and partnering with stakeholders to influence decision-making in a purpose-driven organisation.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n• Support Finance Business Partner with financial analysis, reporting, budgeting, forecasting, and business planning activities\n• Develop predictive analytics and provide insights that support operational and strategic decision-making\n• Identify, analyse, and explain key drivers of financial performance and value creation\n• Monitor business performance against targets and support improvement initiatives\n• Provide commercial and financial decision support to business leaders and stakeholders\n• Challenge assumptions and identify opportunities to improve financial and operational outcomes\n• Ensure compliance with financial policies, processes, and governance requirements\n• Build strong relationships across the portfolio and contribute to a collaborative business partnering culture\n\nAbout You\nYou are an analytical and commercially minded finance professional who enjoys partnering with stakeholders to solve problems and improve business performance. Your ability to build and maintain strong relationships will be critical as you collaborate with a diverse range of stakeholders across the portfolio and broader finance function.\n\nKey Capabilities:\n\n• Bachelor’s degree and post graduate qualifications in a relevant field such as Commerce, Accounting, Finance or Economics. CPA/CA (or progress towards) is preferred.\n• Experience in financial analysis, management reporting, budgeting, forecasting, and business performance analysis\n• Strong analytical skills with the ability to translate complex data into meaningful insights\n• Advanced Excel skills and experience working with financial and reporting systems\n• Excellent communication skills with the ability to present financial information to non-finance stakeholders\n• Strong stakeholder management skills and a collaborative approach to working across teams\n\nWhy work for us?\nTSA offers an inclusive work culture and strong opportunities for career development. In return we also offer benefits such as:\n\n• \nHybrid working environment with 2 days in the office and 3 days working from home\n• \nFree onsite parking\n• \nAn attractive salary including NFP salary packaging ($15,900 tax free) plus meals and entertainment benefits ($2,650)\n• \nPaid parental leave - 12 weeks.\n• \nUp to 8 weeks leave per year through our purchase leave scheme.\n• \nUp to 5 days paid leave per year to 'volunteer' in a TSA program or activity.\n• \nSalvos Rewards - Access to exclusive financial, retail and lifestyle discounts and benefits\n• \nNovated car leasing, discounts on car hire and purchase\n• \nEmployee Assistance Program - Independent confidential counselling service\n\nHow to Apply\nIf you're excited by this unique opportunity, the above sounds like you, and you have a heart for working for an organisation that truly does transform lives, we would love to speak to you. We are looking for compassionate people who share our mission and values. If you have the passion and drive to commit yourself to a challenging and rewarding role; we invite you to apply via the link and submit a current CV and a cover letter which details your alignment with the essential requirements of the role.\n\nApplications will close as soon as a suitable candidate is secured.\n\nThe Salvation Army is an Equal Opportunity Employer who provides an inclusive work environment and embraces the diverse talent of its people. We value and include people of all cultures, languages, abilities, sexual orientations, gender identities, gender expressions and intersex status. We are committed to achieving a diverse workforce and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people.\n\nThe Salvation Army is a child safe organisation and is committed to protecting children and young people from harm. All child facing roles will require the successful completion of a Working with Children Check. Applicants for all roles require a mandatory Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check.\n\nWe value Integrity, Compassion, Respect, Diversity, and Collaboration.","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"finance-analyst-salvationarmy-efczepy4","source_url":"https://salvationarmy.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/broadbean_external/job/Mitcham-VIC-Australia/Finance-Analyst_R60858","source_posted_at":"2026-09-14T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"ecc8b51a-e39d-5074-8b50-6865f9db20ef","company_id":"c785aa0e-063d-5921-8a53-5a4576d6c376","title":"FP&A Analyst","location":"Perth (Whadjuk Country)","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"Global FMCG | Drive financial insights | Manage forecasts, and collaborate with top teams in a dynamic, fast-paced environment\n\nWe are Pernod Ricard, a leading company in the global spirits industry with over 19,000 employees globally. We hold one of the most prestigious and comprehensive brand portfolios in the industry with premium brands including: Absolut vodka, The Glenlivet Scotch whisky, Jameson Irish whiskey, Martell cognac, Havana Club rum, Beefeater, Malfy and Monkey 47 gins, Malibu liqueur and Mumm and Perrier-Jouët champagnes.\n\nThe opportunity\nAs our FP&A Analyst, you’ll play a key role in supporting the financial rhythm of the Australia and New Zealand business ; managing end-to-end forecasting processes and providing critical insights to stakeholders.\nReporting to the Finance Manager, you will play a key role in ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial data, identifying risks and opportunities, and supporting strategic decision-making.\nThis role is ideal for someone with a solid finance foundation, advanced analytical skills, strong Excel skills, great attention to detail, curiosity, and the confidence to work with data, deadlines and multiple stakeholders in a fast-paced environment.\n\nTasks & Responsibilities\n\n• \nManage key forecasting and reporting processes across Australia and New Zealand, from Gross Sales through to Gross Margin.\n• \nSupport monthly and quarterly forecasting cycles, including V2V and Polaris, ensuring inputs are accurate, challenged and delivered on time.\n• \nAnalyse monthly trading performance and help translate results into clear insights, risks, opportunities and recommendations.\n• \nMaintain the accuracy and integrity of key financial dashboards and reporting tools, including V2V and daily sales reporting.\n• \nPartner with Finance, Supply Chain, RGM and Commercial teams to support decision-making and improve forecast quality.\n• \nSupport COGS reporting and forecasting, including actual vs forecast analysis, accruals and communication with internal stakeholders.\n\nWhat you will bring to the role\n\n• \nA tertiary qualification in Commerce, Accounting, Finance or a related discipline.\n• \n3+ years FMCG or industry experience is desirable\n• \nStrong Excel skills, Power Query and Power BI and confidence working with large data sets; PowerPoint skills to help communicate insights clearly.\n• \nStrong attention to detail, with the ability to manage deadlines and follow through on recurring reporting processes.\n• \nA curious and analytical mindset, with the confidence to question numbers and understand what is driving performance.\n• \nClear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work with stakeholders across Finance, Supply Chain and Commercial teams.\n• \nA proactive attitude, willingness to learn and interest in improving how reports, tools and processes work.\n\nConviviality: the Pernod Ricard Way\nWorking at Pernod Ricard is all about igniting conviviality in all that we do. Derived from the French word, convivialité…it means human connection, authenticity, friendship, and fun. Conviviality is energy, spirit and charisma, and is a core philosophy around how we live and work at Pernod Ricard. \nGuided by our four core values; we are team players, dream makers, trailblazers, movers and (cocktail) shakers. We have a passion for living life to the fullest, making new friends every day, and realizing our potential as people and as a business! \nWe know that happiness at work starts with that feeling of belonging you get from an inclusive culture where being uniquely you is celebrated. Our values are lived, they drive our behaviours, and it’s what brings our culture to life. \nOur work philosophy celebrates the magic of human connection with the flexibility needed to provide one's most meaningful contribution. We offer a flexible work policy, with most of our positions offering a hybrid option with flexibility to work remotely 2 days a week.\n\nOur mix of benefits\nProduct allowance | Hybrid and flexible working | Summer hours | Employee Assistance Program | Generous parental leave policy | Career development | Office drinks & events | Inclusive culture ERG |\n\nJoining and contributing to an Inclusive workplace\nAs Créateurs de Convivialité, we are committed to better reflect the richness of our society, the marketplace, and communities in which we operate. We believe that it is the best way to build effective teams, understand our consumers by market and sustainably grow our business.\nPernod Ricard is part of Forbes World’s Best Employers and has been recognized by Equileap among the top 100 Employers for Gender Equality. As a skills-based organization, we ensure fair processes and equal opportunities for all candidates and team members by assessing your skills against role expectations. We recognize that some of you might need extra support with your application, require accommodations or special arrangements for your interview, if this is the case, please contact us, we would be delighted to support you and welcome your application.\n\nJob Posting End Date:\n\nTarget Hire Date:2026-09-14\n\nTarget End Date:","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"fp-a-analyst-pernodricard-datwjr3o","source_url":"https://pernodricard.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/pernod-ricard/job/Perth-Whadjuk-Country/FP-A-Analyst_JR-054958","source_posted_at":"2026-09-14T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"997ab185-012c-539a-8296-258528cefa00","company_id":"b23e985d-adc3-524c-b089-c374c72cbf98","title":"AI Business Analyst, Financial Markets","location":"Sydney","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"• \nHybrid work environment\n• \nBased at our head office in Sydney CBD \n• \nPermanent role \n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated, AI-savvy Business Analyst to join our Financial Markets Business Support Services team and play a pivotal role in delivering strategic business and technology initiatives across trading, risk, operations and settlements.\n\nWorking as part of cross-functional Agile teams, you will partner with business stakeholders, Product Owners, architects, and delivery teams to define, prioritise, and deliver innovative solutions that enhance business capabilities and create tangible customer and operational value.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity for an experienced Business Analyst with financial markets expertise, strong Agile delivery experience, and a passion for using AI and automation to solve complex problems, drive innovation, and deliver business outcomes.\n\nThe Opportunity\nAs an AI-savvy Business Analyst, you will:\n\n• \nDrive requirements discovery and business analysis activities within Agile delivery teams.\n• \nCollaborate closely with Product Owners to refine and prioritise product backlogs.\n• \nTranslate business needs into high-quality user stories, acceptance criteria, and functional requirements.\n• \nFacilitate workshops, story mapping sessions, process reviews, and stakeholder engagements.\n• \nWork across front office, middle office, settlements, operations, risk, and technology teams.\n• \nAnalyse business processes and identify opportunities for continuous improvement.\n• \nChampion the adoption of AI, automation and emerging technologies to drive innovation and improve business outcomes.\n• \nEnsure solutions align with strategic objectives, architecture standards, and regulatory requirements.\n• \nParticipate in sprint planning, backlog refinement, reviews, retrospectives, and release activities.\n• \nChampion Agile best practices and help foster a collaborative, delivery-focused culture.\n\nWhat Success Looks Like\nAs an AI-Savvy Business Analyst, you will be seen as a trusted partner who:\n\n• \nBridges the gap between business and technology.\n• \nLeverages AI tools and automation to streamline processes, reduce manual effort, and increase team productivity.\n• \nDrives clarity and alignment across diverse stakeholder groups.\n• \nDelivers high-quality requirements that accelerate delivery.\n• \nEnables Agile teams to achieve better business outcomes.\n• \nContributes to a culture of continuous improvement and innovation.\n\nAbout You\nYou are an experienced AI-Savvy Business Analyst who thrives in dynamic environments and enjoys turning complex business challenges into practical solutions. You champion the adoption of AI, automation, and emerging technologies to drive innovation and improve business outcomes.\n\nSkills & Experience\n\n• \nBusiness Analysis experience within banking, capital markets, investment management, or financial services.\n• \nDemonstrated experience with harnessing automation and AI tools to simplify complexity, improve productivity, and deliver business value.\n• \nStrong experience working within Agile delivery frameworks such as Scrum, Kanban, or hybrid Agile models.\n• \nDemonstrated experience supporting Product Owners and Agile delivery teams.\n• \nProven capability in writing user stories, defining acceptance criteria, and managing backlogs.\n• \nExcellent stakeholder engagement and facilitation skills.\n• \nStrong analytical and problem-solving abilities.\n• \nStrong understanding of software development lifecycle and iterative delivery practices.\n• \nFinancial Markets experience including fixed income, foreign exchange, listed and OTC derivatives, market data platforms, clearing and settlement, and risk and regulatory reporting is desirable.\n• \nDemonstrated working experience using JIRA, Confluence, SQL and business process modelling tools is highly advantageous.\n\nBe More\nWorking for an organisation that truly makes a difference to the people of Australia, we can offer development and career opportunities in a collaborative environment that supports your growth, wellbeing and promotes flexibility. Your individual growth and success drives the RBA forward as an organisation. Be more means you can do more, for yourself and for Australia.\n\nWhy RBA?\nThe RBA makes an important contribution to the Australian economy through the pursuit of national economic policy objectives and associated activities in financial markets and banking. We also issue Australia's banknotes and operate infrastructure critical to the payments system, all of which contribute to the welfare of the Australian people.\n\nMade up of specialists across a wide range of fields, our people, values, and culture play a critical role in achieving our objectives. Striving to be Open & Dynamic, we consider and incorporate different perspectives, work across teams and are transparent with each other, whilst delivering quality together effectively and focusing on outcomes by prioritising, testing, learning, and refining as we go.\n\nOur people conduct themselves with a high degree of integrity, while striving for excellence in the work they perform and the outcomes they achieve. We encourage intelligent inquiry, and we treat one another with respect while promoting the public interest through our efforts. We know it is the growth and success of our people that drives the RBA forward.\nCome and make a bigger contribution while you build and develop your own skills too, because being more means you can do more, for yourself and for Australia.\n\nThe Reserve Bank of Australia is committed to equity, diversity and inclusion through key initiatives. We welcome and encourage applicants from diverse backgrounds to apply, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, culturally and linguistically diverse background, those living with a disability and from the LGBTQ+ community. We are committed to making the recruitment process fair and equitable for all our candidates.\n\nApplication Close :October 09, 2026\n.","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"ai-business-analyst-financial-markets-rba-buv2odlw","source_url":"https://rba.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/RBA_Careers/job/Sydney/AI-Business-Analyst--Financial-Markets_JR4923","source_posted_at":"2026-09-11T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"43832bc5-2320-5df1-adb1-861faede9514","company_id":"9f400cba-5d3b-5afe-a99e-d8faeaa2b394","title":"Financial Operations Analyst","location":"Minchinbury, NSW, au","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"Grow your career with a global retailer as an Analyst within our Financial Accounting team at ALDI Australia, based in Minchinbury. This is a full-time permanent position.\nAs part of our Financial Accounting team, you will be part of a high performing and results driven team with a focus on process, diligence, and accuracy. A key aspect of this role will see you analysing inventory data and financial transactions to provide insights for continuous improvement.\nCome join us at ALDI, a place where your financial acumen can make a real difference to real people.\nWhat does the role look like? \n\n• Analyse and resolve variances or irregularities across transactional data to ensure accuracy and compliance with internal policies. \n• Troubleshoot and investigate discrepancies by liaising with various stakeholders to reach solutions in a timely manner.\n• Perform month end accounting activities including clearing adjustments and balance sheet reconciliations.\n• Identify process inefficiencies and implement enhancements to strengthen accuracy and control.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams around executing new financial processes.\n• Prepare financial and ad hoc reporting and analyses.\n\n• Previous experience in in business, accounting or related fields.\n• Demonstrated experience using SAP to accurately process, maintain, and manage data, with a high level of attention to detail and commitment to data integrity.\n• Strong communication skills, attention to detail and organisational skills.\n• Excellent problem-solving skills with the ability to liaise work with stakeholders at various levels.\n• Proven ability to adapt to new technologies and systems, with a curious mindset and commitment to continuous learning and improvement.\n• Experience with Inventory Costing (MAP) highly desirable.\n\n• Enjoy 5 weeks annual leave for pursuing your passions outside of work.\n• Enjoy the flexibility of hybrid work options.\n• Support during life’s most important moments including paid parental leave, including superannuation on parental leave.\n• Complimentary access to free physiotherapy to treat non-work related aches, pains or niggles.\n• Work with a company who has been recognised as an Employer of Choice every year since 2018 - 2024.\n• Boost your wellbeing with the MyALDI wellbeing program with discounted access to Fitness Passport and health insurance.\nRemuneration\n\n• Transparent tiered salary range of $143,400 - $163,500 including Superannuation.\nAt ALDI, we celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, abilities, and identities. To learn more, please visit","source_board":"freehire:smartrecruiters","source_external_id":"financial-operations-analyst-aldistores-75mp5yxn","source_url":"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/ALDIStores/744000146888994-financial-operations-analyst","source_posted_at":"2026-09-02T04:58:56Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"fc6bccae-5698-54d9-ac88-ce3c88eb6912","company_id":"e0894684-0270-5393-81b3-2a64e73bfef8","title":"Finance Analyst - Warehouse & Logistics","location":"Melbourne, VIC","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"At Saputo, we bring good to the table by making high-quality products, investing in our people, and supporting communities around the world . As a top 10 global dairy processor, we value contributions that matter and strive to foster an inclusive, growth-driven work environment. Ready to bring your best?\n\nHow you will make contributions that matter\nJoin Saputo Dairy Australia as a Finance Analyst - Warehouse, based at our Southbank office. Reporting to the Finance Manager - Supply Chain, you will provide financial analysis, reporting, forecasting and commercial support across our warehouse operations, including internal and third-party logistics activities.\n\nKey elements of your role will include:\n\n• Partnering with warehouse leaders and operational stakeholders to provide commercial insights and financial analysis\n• Leading budgeting and forecasting activities across warehouse and 3PL operations\n• Delivering weekly and monthly reporting, variance analysis and KPI dashboards\n• Monitoring warehouse costs and identifying risks, opportunities and cost efficiencies\n• Developing financial models to support operational planning and decision-making\n• Supporting business cases, capital projects and continuous improvement initiatives\n• Validating 3PL costs and invoices to improve transparency and cost accuracy\n• Maintaining strong financial controls, governance and reporting integrity\n• Providing financial support across Supply Chain, Commercial, FP&A and S&OP\n\nAbout you\n\n• CA or CPA qualification (Or working towards)\n• Experience in finance, logistics, warehouse operations or supply chain finance\n• Demonstrated experience partnering with operational stakeholders\n• Strong commercial understanding of warehouse, supply chain and 3PL cost structures\n• Advanced financial modelling, variance analysis and KPI reporting skills\n• Advanced Microsoft Excel capability\n• SAP or similar ERP experience\n• Strong communication, stakeholder management and problem-solving skills\n• A proactive approach and genuine focus on continuous improvement\n\nWe’ll support you with\n\n• The opportunity to make contributions that matter, while being supported by a multinational, values-led company\n• A competitive annual salary\n• Learning and development opportunities with the ability to grow in your own way\n• Flexible working arrangements\n• The ability to participate in our Employee Share Ownership Program\n\nClick on Apply for this job to submit your application. \nSaputo Dairy Australia is an equal opportunity employer. All applicants require Australian working rights at the time of applying. \n\nAs a leading dairy processor in Australia, Saputo produces, markets, and distributes a variety of products, with a portfolio of well-loved brands such as Devondale, Liddells, CHEER, Mersey Valley and Tasmanian Heritage. Our people bring these popular brands to life, while servicing our farming communities and through our AG Warehouse network. \n\nWhether your expertise lies in manufacturing, operations, supply chain, sales, quality assurance, or in any other function, your role is integral to our success. You will make contributions that matter, all while working alongside colleagues who genuinely care about your success and who will roll up their sleeves to help.","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"finance-analyst-warehouse-logistics-saputo-wnoatwrh","source_url":"https://saputo.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Saputo_External_Careers/job/Melbourne-VIC/Finance-Analyst---Warehouse---Logistics_JR65362","source_posted_at":"2026-08-28T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"f649d186-fbd5-5d18-853f-0e9b8ff8ef06","company_id":"e0de15a0-f04a-5191-a853-0b2087d1e1e6","title":"Financial System Analyst","location":"Rockhampton, Rockhampton & Capricorn Coast QLD","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"Salary: $107,154 – $111,619 per year\nFinancial System Analyst\n\n• \nPermanent / Full Time\n• \nMonday to Friday, 72.5 hours per fortnight, 9 day fortnight\n• \n$107,154 - $111,619 per annum (LGIA Stream A) Level 5 or $98,633 - $104,913 Level 4 (dependent on skills and experience) + Superannuation\n• \nLocation – Rockhampton\nYour new role\nAre you passionate about financial systems, data analysis, and delivering solutions that support organisational success?\nRockhampton Regional Council is seeking a Financial Systems Officer to join our Finance team. Working within the Financial Systems Unit, you will play a key role in supporting, maintaining, and enhancing Council's finance systems, reporting capabilities, and business processes.\nWorking as part of a collaborative team, you will assist with system upgrades, integrations, reporting development, data analysis, and user support across Council's financial systems. Your work will help ensure the accuracy, integrity, and security of critical financial information while contributing to continuous improvement initiatives and informed decision-making.\nThis is an exciting opportunity for an analytical and customer-focused professional who enjoys combining financial knowledge with technology and systems expertise.\nThis position requires the completion of a satisfactory Criminal History Check - Police Certificate (Australia Wide Name Only Police Check).\nWhat we are looking for\n\n• \nRelevant Industry experience and/or qualifications in Accounting, Business, Information Technology.\n• \nSound knowledge of Accounting Standards, financial management principles, and enterprise business systems.\n• \nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to troubleshoot system issues and implement effective solutions.\n• \nExcellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to manage priorities, meet deadlines, and work collaboratively within a team.\nWhat you'll get in return\nAs an employee of Rockhampton Regional Council, you will join a diverse and innovative team of more than 1000 employees supported by good leadership, who proudly deliver services and make a difference to the lives of people living and working within the region.\n\n• \nSupportive Work/Life Balance\n• \nA large employer with a strong values driven culture\n• \n12% employer superannuation contribution, with the option to salary sacrifice up to an additional 6%\n• \nOngoing training and development opportunities\n• \nCorporate membership discounts\n• \nPayroll deductions and salary sacrifice options\n• \n17.5% annual leave loading\n• \nWages paid fortnightly\n• \nEmployee Assistance Program\n• \nFitness Passport and active social clubs \nWhat you need to do next\nTo apply for this opportunity, please submit two documents:\n\n• \nA 2-3 page Cover Letter addressing the Application Criteria below;\n• \nYour Current resume.\nApplication Criteria\n\n• \nDemonstrated experience in financial systems administration, reporting, and data analysis, with the ability to identify issues and implement effective solutions.\n• \nProven ability to develop and enhance financial reports and data extracts that support operational and business requirements.\n• \nSound knowledge of Accounting Standards, financial principles, and system controls, with strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n• \nStrong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to provide professional advice, drive continuous improvement, and manage competing priorities.\nPlease use Council’s cover letter template and ensure you clearly label each Application Criteria in your cover letter.\nClick the ‘Apply’ button to complete your online application.\nApplications Close: Monday 31 August 2026 at Midnight (AEST)","source_board":"freehire:seek","source_external_id":"financial-system-analyst-rockhampton-regional-council-ec5uuohx","source_url":"https://www.seek.com.au/job/93969728","source_posted_at":"2026-08-14T00:44:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"3054b9ae-e865-51a0-9b43-4e7bd9be405f","company_id":"d8e9385a-1e0b-5068-982b-78b59a389aed","title":"Finance Analyst","location":"Melbourne, Victoria","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"Finance Analyst \nWe are growing fast and looking for a dynamic Finance Analyst to help manage and maintain relevant financials and commercial leasing arrangements across the organisation.\nThis role is responsible for supporting the Management Accounting team through the preparation, analysis, and reporting of financial information to facilitate effective business decision-making. The role includes completing month-end close activities, preparing and reviewing profit and loss statements, analysing variances against budget and forecast, preparing balance sheet reconciliations, and investigating reconciling items. The Finance Analyst partners with stakeholders across the business to communicate financial insights, improve financial performance, and ensure accurate, timely, and compliant financial reporting while maintaining strong attention to detail and organisational skills consistently.\nRole Purpose\n\n• To work as part of the Management Accounting team to achieve the completion of an accurate and timely month-end close to assist key stakeholders with decision making.\n• To analyse monthly results and partner with various stakeholders across the business to identify favourable and unfavourable variances against forecast and advise stakeholders on areas for improvement.\n• Responsible for the preparation of balance sheet reconciliations, including investigation of material reconciling items\n\nResponsibilities \n\n• Prepare and finalise monthly profit and loss (P&L) statements for venues\n• Analysis of monthly venue profit and loss statements\n• Review and analyse labour costs and operating expense accruals\n• Analyse monthly P&L results and explain variances against budget\n• Develop strong relationships with business stakeholders\n• Communicate financial insights and findings to key stakeholders\n• Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders and finance team members\n• Review weekly P&L performance against budget and identify variances\n• Prepare balance sheet reconciliations and investigate/reconcile material variances\n\nWhat we need from you \n\n• Technical or functional expertise including excellent numeracy skills\n• Accuracy and attention to detail\n• Effective organisation and time management skills.\n• Ability and desire to grow with the organisation.\n• Analytical and problem-solving skills.\n• High level of drive, motivation, initiative and resilience.\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills\n• Honesty, integrity and trust\n• Ability to work in a team\n\nExperience and Background \n\n• Bachelor’s degree majoring in finance\n• A minimum of 12 months of practical experience within a large or mid-tier accounting firm or a similar role in industry\n• Studying towards CA or CPA preferred\n\nSalary range from $85,000 to $95,000 depending on experience.","source_board":"freehire:workday","source_external_id":"finance-analyst-avc-technology-corporation-nszc677s","source_url":"https://ausvenueco.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/AVC/job/Melbourne-Victoria/Finance-Analyst_JR102078","source_posted_at":"2026-07-21T00:00:00Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"f159b17c-2cc5-5a09-8f9f-71d8a9814ca6","company_id":"58d05a5c-3bb2-5604-b95b-242fec475c8c","title":"Finance Business Analyst","location":"Melbourne, Melbourne Region","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from adzuna; read the complete posting at https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5889615668\n\nOur client is a well renowned, global leader in the sports and retail industry. They are seeking a highly motivated finance professional who has a keen eye for detail and desire to probe further into data. The Business Analyst will report to the Director of Finance and will manage the day-to-day financial aspects of the business. Key responsibilities of the role- Building & supporting business critical reports using Power BI Supporting Sales team with data and analytics Comfort in manipulating …","source_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5889615668","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5889615668","source_posted_at":"2026-09-19T02:43:00Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"881457d5-9f99-5767-aab9-98807ee64ccb","company_id":"da178996-441b-5ab2-a782-5414b40a1120","title":"Financial Analyst","location":"The Rocks, Sydney","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from adzuna; read the complete posting at https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5889433432\n\nAbout Us: At Fitness Passport, we are driven by a clear purpose — to make fitness more accessible, so more people can lead active and healthier lives. Established in 2006, we’re a corporate heal