rce_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5805480664","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5805480664","source_posted_at":"2026-07-18T10:15:27Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"7f9ff0a7-fca3-5a2f-97a5-2f6e85c59187","company_id":"5f1d9e00-1c40-58e3-be5c-ac2b53a79a8e","title":"Reporting Analyst - Data Warehouse Hybrid","location":"The Rocks, Sydney","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Finance","career_id":null,"experience_level":"not stated","description":"JD excerpt from adzuna; read the complete posting at https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5802032372\n\nJoin Unity Bank as a Reporting Analyst - Data Warehouse and play a critical role in strengthening the bank’s data, reporting, and analytics capability. This is a key hands-on role for a technically strong data professional who can design and optimise data pipelines, improve reporting reliability, and deliver trusted insights that support regulatory obligations, operational performance, and executive decision-making. You will work across SQL, Azure, Power BI, and enterprise data platforms to hel…","source_board":"adzuna","source_external_id":"5802032372","source_url":"https://www.adzuna.com.au/details/5802032372","source_posted_at":"2026-07-16T11:05:01Z","description_is_excerpt":true,"source_group":"finance_analyst"},{"id":"18645685-62ea-5f2f-a2ad-1d774c4c6cbc","company_id":"d49d6717-4bdb-501d-b55d-d6b9118c69f1","title":"Social Media with Admin and Bookkeeping Experience","location":"Sydney, NSW, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Accounting & Audit","career_id":null,"experience_level":"1 years minimum","description":"Job Title: Social Media with Admin and Bookkeeping Experience\n\nClient: Australian\n\nWork Hours: 20 hours week\n\nVA rate: $5/hour\n\nJob Description:\n\nThe client has pet product and wellness brand, is seeking a creative, organized, and proactive Virtual Assistant to support their growing business. The VA will play a key role in managing the brands social media presence, handling administrative tasks, and assisting with basic graphic design. This is a remote position for individuals who love pets, understand content marketing, and have a flair for visual storytelling.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\nSocial Media Management\n\n• Create and schedule engaging, pet-related content for Instagram and Facebook\n• Organize weekly and monthly content calendars using Canva\n• Monitor engagement and respond to comments/messages professionally\n• Repurpose client-supplied photos and videos into branded, high-quality posts\n• Track content performance and provide insights or suggestions for improvement\n\nGraphic Design & Content Creation\n\n• Format marketing materials, social posts, and simple digital assets using Canva\n• Design aesthetically pleasing and on-brand visuals to promote products and pet wellness content\n\nAdministrative Support\n\n• Maintain and update spreadsheets (e.g., inventory, content tracking, client records)\n• Assist with email communication and simple bookkeeping tasks\n• Prepare reports or summaries upon request\n• Format documents and internal files as needed\n\nRequirements & Expectations:\n\n• Strong command of written and spoken English\n• 1+ year of experience in social media management (Instagram, Facebook preferred)\n• Skilled in Canva and comfortable designing marketing creatives\n• Reliable internet connection and availability for weekly check-ins\n• Highly organized with the ability to multitask and meet deadlines\n• Passion for pets and interest in wellness-related topics is a plus\n• Willing to take initiative and bring creative content ideas to the table\n• Must be able to start immediately and commit to a minimum of 20 hours/week\n• Availability to attend a video call interview with the client during the onboarding process\n\nTo Apply:\n\nPlease submit your resume and a portfolio of relevant experience and availability.\n\nApply here:","source_board":"freehire:manatal","source_external_id":"social-media-with-admin-and-bookkeeping-experience-gentask-virtual-assistance-services-3qrqa57r","source_url":"https://www.careers-page.com/gentask-virtual-assistance-services/job/L9Y93V44","source_posted_at":"2026-09-14T16:09:15Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"accounting"},{"id":"e8ed0e82-76e8-5b83-a3aa-7561dd153232","company_id":"d49d6717-4bdb-501d-b55d-d6b9118c69f1","title":"Virtual Assistant (Customer Support, Admin, SEO, Bookkeeping)","location":"QLD, Australia","job_type":"full_time","industry":"Accounting & Audit","career_id":null,"experience_level":"entry-level title","description":"Job Title: Full-Time Virtual Assistant (Customer Support, Admin, SEO, Bookkeeping)\n\nJob Description:\nWe are seeking a highly organized and proactive Full-Time Virtual Assistant. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, communicates effectively, and is passionate about supporting small business operations. The assistant will support day-to-day administrative needs, ensure timely customer service, maintain website content, and assist with light bookkeeping and SEO tasks.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\nCustomer Service & Communication\n\n• Respond to customer support emails and website chat in a timely and professional manner\n• Maintain a helpful, solution-focused tone with customers to support sales efforts\n\nWebsite & Marketing Support\n\n• Update and maintain website content as needed (non-technical)\n• Set up and manage Klaviyo email support channels\n• Assist in SEO-optimized blog writing (product tips, tutorials, updates)\n\nAdministrative Tasks\n\n• General admin support such as organizing files, documentation, and scheduling\n• Proactively flag any issues or process challenges to management\n\nBookkeeping\n\n• Perform basic bookkeeping tasks including Xero reconciliation (training provided if needed)\n\nQualifications:\n\n• Proven experience in administrative support and customer service (preferably eCommerce or service-based businesses)\n• Experience with Klaviyo (or similar email platforms) is a strong plus\n• Familiarity with SEO and blog writing is preferred\n• Basic understanding of Xero or willingness to learn\n• Strong English communication skills (verbal and written)\n• Excellent time management and organizational abilities\n• High level of integrity and accountability\n• Must be proactive and transparent in communicating issues and progress\n\nWorking Hours:\n\n• 10:00 AM 4:00 PM Manila Time (Monday to Friday)\n• Weekend availability TBD based on customer inquiry volume","source_board":"freehire:manatal","source_external_id":"virtual-assistant-customer-support-admin-seo-bookkeeping-gentask-virtual-assistance-services-62e2tvr7","source_url":"https://www.careers-page.com/gentask-virtual-assistance-services/job/QVVR33V8","source_posted_at":"2026-09-14T16:09:15Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"accounting"},{"id":"c081c7c2-afd4-5a97-aa13-a96029b41e2e","company_id":"d3721735-704b-516b-964f-6ab8334948f3","title":"Accounting Intern","location":"Bella Vista, Australia","job_type":"internship","industry":"Accounting & Audit","career_id":null,"experience_level":"intern","description":"Job Description: We are seeking a highly motivated and eager Accounting Intern to assist with bookkeeping tasks, financial reporting, and other accounting duties. The ideal candidate will have a strong interest in accounting, excellent analytical skills, and a desire to learn and grow in a professional environment.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n• \nAssist in maintaining accurate financial records and ensuring compliance with accounting standards.\n\n• \nHelp prepare financial statements, including balance sheets, income statements, and cash flow statements.\n\n• \nSupport budgeting, forecasting, and financial planning activities.\n\n• \nAssist with accounts payable and receivable, payroll processing, and tax filing.\n\n• \nConduct regular audits and reconciliations to ensure accuracy and compliance.\n\n• \nProvide support for financial analysis and reporting to management.\n\n• \nMaintain confidentiality and integrity of financial information.\n\nRequirements\nRequirements:\n\n• \nBachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field.\n\n• \nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n• \nExcellent communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n• \nProficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word, PowerPoint).\n\n• \nAbility to work independently and manage multiple tasks simultaneously.\n\n• \nA keen interest in accounting and finance.\n\nBenefits\nBenefits:\n\n• \nHands-on experience in a professional accounting environment.\n\n• \nMentorship and guidance from experienced accounting professionals.\n\n• \nOpportunity to learn and develop new skills.\n\n• \nFlexible working hours to accommodate academic commitments.\n\n• \nPotential for future full-time employment based on performance.","source_board":"freehire:zohorecruit","source_external_id":"accounting-intern-it-support-guy-km4legx5","source_url":"https://itsupportguy.zohorecruit.com.au/jobs/Careers/10920000000480004","source_posted_at":"2026-09-02T13:32:19Z","description_is_excerpt":false,"source_group":"accounting"},{"id":"93812fb4-66bd-5471-a49d-a301be06d22b","company_id":"ca669c92-e816-5399-b9b4-553aefa00255","title":"Accounting Intern - Adelaide, SA","location":"Adelaide, South Australia, Australia","job_type":"internship","industry":"Accounting & Audit","career_id":null,"experience_level":"intern","description":"About the Host & Role Overview\n\nOur host company operates within the various but relevant sector and provides valuable opportunities for graduates and emerging professionals to gain practical industry experience in their field where you get an opportunity to gain hands-on experience, develop industry-relevant skills, and work alongside experienced professionals in a real workplace environment (onsite, remote, or project-based). \n\nKey Learning Responsibilities\n\n• Prepare and maintain financial records for accuracy and completeness.\n• Reconcile bank statements and accounts regularly to ensure consistency.\n• Record day-to-day financial transactions and ensure they are accurately logged in the accounting system.\n• Using accounting software (XERO, MYOB, Quickbooks) to generate accounting reports\n• Process accounts payable and accounts receivable in a timely manner.\n• Ensure compliance with accounting policies, tax regulations, and internal controls.\n• Manage trust accounting for property management and sales systems, including receipting and reconciliation.\n• Process payroll and ensure accurate deductions, payments, and reporting.\n• Provide administrative support, including filing, handling inquiries, and general bookkeeping tasks.\n\nSkills & Attributes\n\n• Positive attitude and willingness to learn\n• Robust communication and interpersonal skills\n• Ability to work collaboratively\n• Good organisational and time management skills\n• Relevant educational background, training, or interest in the industry\n\nBenefits of our Voluntary Professional Career Internship Program\n\n• Hands-on industry exposure to bridge the gap between education and employment with flexibility on a part time basis.\n• There may be a high potential for securing a job following the completion of the internship for the right talent.\n• The placement fee is the lowest possible and is only if a successful placement is secured; there are no registration fees.\n• You will have the opportunity to work alongside professionals in your industry, expanding your network, competencies, and career growth.\n• This internship offers a wealth of knowledge and transferable skills that you can gain, and the host company will provide you with a work experience letter.\n\nDisclaimer: Placement opportunities are subject to candidate suitability, host company requirements, availability, and our Terms and Conditions. Internship and employment outcomes are not guar